1
00:00:00,367 --> 00:00:01,767
(Chiang Mai)

2
00:00:01,768 --> 00:00:05,371
(Flying from Chiang Mai to Bangkok)

3
00:00:06,306 --> 00:00:09,475
(Arriving in Singapore for their layover)

4
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:14,113
(Singapore Changi Airport)

5
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:16,949
We're in Singapore now.

6
00:00:17,251 --> 00:00:19,385
(Cheering)

7
00:00:19,386 --> 00:00:21,954
I don't know how we got here.
We woke up at dawn.

8
00:00:21,955 --> 00:00:23,388
Our original flight got canceled,

9
00:00:23,389 --> 00:00:24,757
so we're having a bit of a rough time.

10
00:00:24,758 --> 00:00:25,659
Right.

11
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:27,560
Finally, this is going to be
our last flight.

12
00:00:27,561 --> 00:00:28,828
We're going to Medan.

13
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:31,164
- Our last flight.
- Seriously.

14
00:00:31,165 --> 00:00:32,565
(Finally going to Medan
after three different cities)

15
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:34,934
We could've had more free time,

16
00:00:35,135 --> 00:00:37,770
but we'll be arriving at 3 p.m.

17
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:40,005
We'll spend one night in Medan,

18
00:00:40,174 --> 00:00:41,841
then head to the jungle the next day.

19
00:00:41,842 --> 00:00:43,243
Bukit Lawang!

20
00:00:43,811 --> 00:00:45,145
Bukit Lawang!

21
00:00:45,146 --> 00:00:46,112
Bukit Lawang.

22
00:00:46,113 --> 00:00:49,616
I looked up a few places and picked one.

23
00:00:49,617 --> 00:00:51,418
- Already?
- We're going to pick one.

24
00:00:52,085 --> 00:00:54,420
To be exact, we're going to pick one.

25
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,888
We got a lot closer.

26
00:00:55,889 --> 00:00:57,289
- Yes.
- We did.

27
00:00:57,558 --> 00:01:00,759
- How about one room for all of us?
- That sounds good.

28
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,961
Let me check.

29
00:01:02,962 --> 00:01:05,697
How did you like sharing one room?

30
00:01:05,698 --> 00:01:07,967
Since we're sharing one suitcase...

31
00:01:07,968 --> 00:01:10,402
- It's sad when we have separate rooms.
- It's inconvenient.

32
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:12,204
Right. One room is better.

33
00:01:12,673 --> 00:01:13,706
Since we have one suitcase.

34
00:01:13,707 --> 00:01:14,941
What do you think about this place?

35
00:01:16,443 --> 00:01:17,410
- I like it.
- Really?

36
00:01:17,445 --> 00:01:18,211
What is that?

37
00:01:18,212 --> 00:01:21,281
- It looks fancy.
- It looks like an apartment.

38
00:01:21,282 --> 00:01:24,017
- We need to recharge.
- I love it.

39
00:01:24,018 --> 00:01:25,418
Let's go for an apartment-style room.

40
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:28,058
- To get a taste of the city.
- A taste of the city.

41
00:01:28,059 --> 00:01:29,122
A taste of cement.

42
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:30,089
- I like it.
- Sounds good.

43
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:32,225
I'll book it!

44
00:01:32,226 --> 00:01:33,593
Let's pay!

45
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:34,927
(Laughing)

46
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:35,861
Done.

47
00:01:36,096 --> 00:01:37,329
That was fast.

48
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:38,464
That was so fast.

49
00:01:38,632 --> 00:01:39,599
Super easy.

50
00:01:39,935 --> 00:01:41,367
I do this all the time.

51
00:01:41,368 --> 00:01:44,003
Booking things is basically my life.

52
00:01:44,172 --> 00:01:47,206
When we arrive in Medan,
let's buy some things...

53
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,175
we might need in the jungle.

54
00:01:49,176 --> 00:01:50,376
We need a lot of things.

55
00:01:50,377 --> 00:01:52,345
We're out of shampoo too.

56
00:01:52,346 --> 00:01:53,380
Right.

57
00:01:53,381 --> 00:01:55,148
That sounds good. By the way,

58
00:01:55,582 --> 00:01:56,715
we could buy some things here.

59
00:01:56,716 --> 00:01:59,685
They have nice stores here.

60
00:01:59,686 --> 00:02:01,420
We could buy one item here.

61
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:02,955
- At least one.
- Yes.

62
00:02:03,223 --> 00:02:06,225
We can at least buy one carefully.

63
00:02:06,226 --> 00:02:08,960
- Right.
- We need to buy one item for the jungle.

64
00:02:08,961 --> 00:02:10,329
We sweat so much.

65
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:13,199
- Boarding starts at 2 p.m.
- We only have 30 minutes left.

66
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,234
Let's hurry.

67
00:02:14,235 --> 00:02:15,568
- Let's get going.
- Okay.

68
00:02:15,569 --> 00:02:16,972
We have 30 minutes.

69
00:02:16,973 --> 00:02:19,305
- We don't have time.
- Okay.

70
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,908
(On their way to go shopping)

71
00:02:22,075 --> 00:02:23,776
(Dancing)

72
00:02:23,911 --> 00:02:24,744
Oh, my.

73
00:02:25,472 --> 00:02:28,841
Singapore Airport has
great duty-free shops.

74
00:02:29,850 --> 00:02:31,450
Look at those bags.

75
00:02:31,451 --> 00:02:33,252
(Luxury brands everywhere!)

76
00:02:33,253 --> 00:02:35,755
I have something to show you.

77
00:02:35,889 --> 00:02:37,556
- Could you hold it for a moment?
- Okay.

78
00:02:40,294 --> 00:02:41,628
Mosquito bites.

79
00:02:41,629 --> 00:02:43,429
- Mosquito bites.
- Mosquito bites.

80
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:45,164
Mosquito bites.

81
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:46,266
So...

82
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:48,901
I'm going to wear long pants
in the jungle.

83
00:02:49,236 --> 00:02:50,137
Me too.

84
00:02:50,138 --> 00:02:52,405
- I should buy long pants.
- There are lots of bugs.

85
00:02:52,706 --> 00:02:53,673
Okay.

86
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:56,542
(They split up to look around.)

87
00:02:56,877 --> 00:02:58,578
(They're excited about shopping.)

88
00:02:58,579 --> 00:03:00,513
Grey really doesn't suit me.

89
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:02,515
Grey doesn't suit you?

90
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:04,850
- It doesn't.
- Bright colors suit you better.

91
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,218
I like this. Should I get one?

92
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:09,888
I saw a lot of dancers wearing that.

93
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:11,123
Really?

94
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:12,692
That's it.

95
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:13,892
(Trying the headband on)

96
00:03:13,893 --> 00:03:15,828
- That's really good.
- You look good.

97
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:17,396
You look good.

98
00:03:17,965 --> 00:03:20,934
(How do I look?)

99
00:03:20,935 --> 00:03:21,834
Now...

100
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,846
Anyway...

101
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:26,706
- Let me try another color.
- Okay.

102
00:03:27,241 --> 00:03:28,207
I can't wait.

103
00:03:28,475 --> 00:03:29,542
I like this one.

104
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:30,977
(Smiling)

105
00:03:30,978 --> 00:03:31,844
(Gasping)

106
00:03:31,845 --> 00:03:33,045
Hi, orangutan.

107
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:34,847
I'm Gabee.

108
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,417
Orangutan, have you been waiting for me?

109
00:03:39,453 --> 00:03:41,821
(What are you doing?)

110
00:03:42,022 --> 00:03:44,023
I should get this one.

111
00:03:44,024 --> 00:03:45,191
I'll get this.

112
00:03:45,192 --> 00:03:46,525
I should get one. I can't help it.

113
00:03:46,526 --> 00:03:47,526
You're cute.

114
00:03:47,795 --> 00:03:50,563
"I should get this one."

115
00:03:50,864 --> 00:03:51,797
(Sian is shopping barefoot.)

116
00:03:51,798 --> 00:03:52,832
I'll try this one.

117
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:54,033
Are you going to buy this?

118
00:03:54,034 --> 00:03:56,469
I'm considering it.

119
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:57,937
It's good that it's performance wear.

120
00:03:57,938 --> 00:04:00,573
- You don't have long pants like that.
- That's true.

121
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:01,440
Get one.

122
00:04:01,441 --> 00:04:04,477
You look like a model now.

123
00:04:04,478 --> 00:04:05,979
She's a model.

124
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,379
(Remembering she's a model)

125
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:09,782
She looks good in that
because it really shows off her figure.

126
00:04:11,718 --> 00:04:13,352
(Twerking with excitement)

127
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:14,253
Hey.

128
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,755
We can have this much fun
just at a shopping mall.

129
00:04:16,756 --> 00:04:18,490
Why do we even need to go to the jungle?

130
00:04:18,491 --> 00:04:20,059
That's crazy.

131
00:04:20,761 --> 00:04:23,096
If I want to look good,
I should wear something tight.

132
00:04:23,097 --> 00:04:24,897
(Enjoying the last taste of civilization)

133
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:26,432
I don't know what to get.

134
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,768
(Looking for an item for the jungle)

135
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:29,736
These four.

136
00:04:29,737 --> 00:04:30,737
(Each picking one item)

137
00:04:30,738 --> 00:04:32,071
One, two, three, four.

138
00:04:32,239 --> 00:04:34,561
We paid for them with our own money.

139
00:04:34,562 --> 00:04:35,875
(Using their own money
instead of the group funds)

140
00:04:36,243 --> 00:04:37,910
(Paid and done)

141
00:04:37,911 --> 00:04:39,579
(Sian: pants, Gabee: a hairband,
Won Ji: a T-shirt, Harimu: pants)

142
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:41,214
Thank you so much.

143
00:04:41,215 --> 00:04:43,349
- Bye.
- Enjoy your jungle.

144
00:04:43,984 --> 00:04:44,951
Good purchase.

145
00:04:44,952 --> 00:04:46,986
We got a little carried away
with shopping.

146
00:04:46,987 --> 00:04:48,054
(Boarding)

147
00:04:48,055 --> 00:04:48,853
(Singapore)

148
00:04:48,854 --> 00:04:54,393
(On their way to their final destination,
Medan)

149
00:04:57,664 --> 00:05:02,167
(Kuala Namu International Airport, Medan)

150
00:05:03,537 --> 00:05:06,606
We've arrived in Indonesia!

151
00:05:08,075 --> 00:05:09,575
A new city.

152
00:05:09,576 --> 00:05:12,045
- A new city.
- I never imagined we'd come to Indonesia.

153
00:05:12,446 --> 00:05:15,681
(Indonesia)

154
00:05:15,682 --> 00:05:19,318
(The world's largest island country,
made up of more than 17,000 islands)

155
00:05:19,686 --> 00:05:22,922
(Where tradition and everyday life
blend together)

156
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,558
(A vast, mysterious land
embraced by Mother Nature)

157
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:32,004
(The starting point for the journey
to Bukit Lawang, home to the orangutans)

158
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:35,467
(Medan)

159
00:05:35,468 --> 00:05:37,336
It took us almost a whole day.

160
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:38,571
We took a huge detour.

161
00:05:38,739 --> 00:05:40,973
So, I looked it up.

162
00:05:40,974 --> 00:05:43,109
It takes two hours
to get to the city by car.

163
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:45,678
It takes too long to get there.

164
00:05:45,679 --> 00:05:47,380
But we can take the airport train.

165
00:05:47,748 --> 00:05:48,948
It only takes 40 minutes.

166
00:05:48,949 --> 00:05:51,984
Let's take the airport train
to get there faster.

167
00:05:51,985 --> 00:05:54,220
- Okay. We don't have enough time.
- Right.

168
00:05:54,387 --> 00:05:55,721
(Checking the train schedule)

169
00:05:55,722 --> 00:05:57,923
- It's 4 p.m. right now.
- It's 4 p.m.

170
00:05:57,924 --> 00:05:59,491
As far as I know,
the train leaves at 4:15 p.m.

171
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:00,325
Really?

172
00:06:00,326 --> 00:06:01,927
Since we might get lost along the way,

173
00:06:01,928 --> 00:06:03,061
we need to hurry.

174
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:05,564
- We're in a rush.
- Everyone.

175
00:06:05,565 --> 00:06:06,431
Yes.

176
00:06:06,432 --> 00:06:08,868
It's 4 p.m. now,
and the train leaves at 4:15 p.m.

177
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:10,870
- Let's hurry.
- Okay.

178
00:06:10,895 --> 00:06:12,328
That must be it.

179
00:06:13,106 --> 00:06:14,440
- We're taking the train.
- Okay.

180
00:06:14,876 --> 00:06:17,510
- We have to hurry.
- We can make it.

181
00:06:17,511 --> 00:06:18,277
Okay.

182
00:06:18,278 --> 00:06:19,745
I hope it's close.

183
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:22,147
It's almost time.

184
00:06:22,172 --> 00:06:24,473
If we miss this one,
we'll have to wait a long time.

185
00:06:25,152 --> 00:06:25,985
(Looking around)

186
00:06:25,986 --> 00:06:27,587
Is that the ticket machine?

187
00:06:27,588 --> 00:06:28,788
It is!

188
00:06:28,789 --> 00:06:30,089
It's here.

189
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,958
It's so brand-new.

190
00:06:31,959 --> 00:06:33,727
- Tickets!
- Hello.

191
00:06:33,728 --> 00:06:36,662
The airport train is right next to it.

192
00:06:36,797 --> 00:06:39,465
- We're four people.
- Four people.

193
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:41,266
- Four people.
- To Medan, right?

194
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:42,501
Yes, Medan.

195
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:44,404
You have 11 minutes left.

196
00:06:44,405 --> 00:06:46,571
If we miss the 4:15 p.m. train,

197
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:48,206
we have to wait for an hour and a half.

198
00:06:48,851 --> 00:06:49,716
We can't do that.

199
00:06:49,741 --> 00:06:51,376
The train comes every hour and a half.

200
00:06:51,645 --> 00:06:53,379
We need to get moving
as soon as we get our tickets.

201
00:06:53,614 --> 00:06:55,448
Thank you.

202
00:06:55,449 --> 00:06:56,315
(Four tickets: 260,000 rupiah)

203
00:06:56,316 --> 00:06:58,417
They look like receipts.

204
00:06:58,952 --> 00:06:59,852
It's cute.

205
00:06:59,853 --> 00:07:01,420
Let's go.

206
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:02,988
We got our tickets.

207
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,223
An orangutan!

208
00:07:04,224 --> 00:07:05,291
It's right there.

209
00:07:05,292 --> 00:07:07,759
- An orangutan!
- It's good to see it!

210
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,361
It looks so scary.

211
00:07:09,362 --> 00:07:10,495
(Welcome!)

212
00:07:10,496 --> 00:07:12,397
- It looks scary.
- Right?

213
00:07:12,398 --> 00:07:13,599
(They can't take their eyes off it.)

214
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,867
Wait.

215
00:07:15,468 --> 00:07:16,935
That's the exit.

216
00:07:17,737 --> 00:07:18,805
I think it's this way.

217
00:07:18,806 --> 00:07:21,173
That's another exit.

218
00:07:21,198 --> 00:07:22,365
Where is it?

219
00:07:23,844 --> 00:07:24,811
This way?

220
00:07:25,212 --> 00:07:26,178
Over there.

221
00:07:26,313 --> 00:07:29,081
There's a ticket booth here.

222
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:31,083
Okay.

223
00:07:31,084 --> 00:07:33,786
The airport train looks small.

224
00:07:34,487 --> 00:07:35,720
It's so compact.

225
00:07:36,590 --> 00:07:38,324
You scan the QR code.

226
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:39,491
(Beeping)

227
00:07:39,492 --> 00:07:40,325
Done.

228
00:07:40,594 --> 00:07:41,594
Thank you.

229
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,630
(Everyone rushed
through the ticket gates.)

230
00:07:44,798 --> 00:07:45,731
That's it!

231
00:07:45,732 --> 00:07:47,433
It's really set up well.

232
00:07:48,235 --> 00:07:49,502
It's so clean.

233
00:07:50,036 --> 00:07:52,404
- It's charming.
- It's not bad.

234
00:07:52,405 --> 00:07:54,206
It looks charming.

235
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,408
It looks more like a train than a subway.

236
00:07:56,409 --> 00:07:58,243
It reminds me of the KTX.

237
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:01,446
Our seats are already assigned.

238
00:08:01,914 --> 00:08:05,350
I'm in Car 3, seat 8A.

239
00:08:06,553 --> 00:08:10,322
(Getting on the airport train)

240
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:12,791
- Should I put the suitcase here?
- Let's put it there.

241
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,460
Let me put it here.

242
00:08:15,485 --> 00:08:18,454
Thank you. Please give me my bag.

243
00:08:19,801 --> 00:08:21,934
We're safe now.

244
00:08:22,969 --> 00:08:24,469
We got on the train safely.

245
00:08:24,905 --> 00:08:26,439
(Sniffing)

246
00:08:26,907 --> 00:08:28,941
(Refreshing themselves
with a little fragrance)

247
00:08:28,942 --> 00:08:30,476
That must be a herbal inhaler too.

248
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:33,846
She looks refreshed.

249
00:08:34,447 --> 00:08:36,081
Do you feel refreshed, ma'am?

250
00:08:36,082 --> 00:08:37,282
(I hope you have a refreshing ride.)

251
00:08:37,851 --> 00:08:41,320
(They're also in their seats.)

252
00:08:41,821 --> 00:08:43,789
Sian, you're really putting them away.

253
00:08:44,224 --> 00:08:45,191
Seriously.

254
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:48,026
(Now that she's relaxed,
she's getting goofy.)

255
00:08:48,027 --> 00:08:49,228
(Laughing)

256
00:08:49,229 --> 00:08:50,529
We're heading out.

257
00:08:51,231 --> 00:08:52,131
Right?

258
00:08:52,341 --> 00:08:55,143
The train is so clean and pleasant.

259
00:08:55,168 --> 00:08:56,101
It's air-conditioned too.

260
00:08:56,102 --> 00:08:57,636
- It's so modern.
- Yes.

261
00:08:58,104 --> 00:08:59,104
This is a modern trip.

262
00:08:59,105 --> 00:09:00,205
I love it.

263
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,807
It's more convenient than I expected...

264
00:09:01,808 --> 00:09:03,875
- because it's connected to the airport.
- It's super close too.

265
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:05,977
I thought we would stand...

266
00:09:05,978 --> 00:09:07,946
like a subway too.

267
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:08,747
Me too.

268
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:11,049
You get an assigned seat like on a train.

269
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:12,684
I really like that.

270
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:14,186
(Having an assigned seat makes
it more pleasant.)

271
00:09:15,088 --> 00:09:16,922
Look at the view.

272
00:09:18,731 --> 00:09:20,231
Our first encounter with Indonesia.

273
00:09:21,763 --> 00:09:23,329
They did a good job with the crops.

274
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:24,864
A good job with the crops?

275
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:29,034
It's so rural here.

276
00:09:29,369 --> 00:09:31,270
They have an agricultural lifestyle here.

277
00:09:31,471 --> 00:09:33,539
It almost looks like no one lives here.

278
00:09:33,873 --> 00:09:35,740
- People do live here.
- You're right.

279
00:09:38,526 --> 00:09:40,112
My goodness.

280
00:09:40,113 --> 00:09:42,114
(Covering her mouth)

281
00:09:42,115 --> 00:09:43,849
I didn't see that.

282
00:09:44,317 --> 00:09:46,385
Of course, people live here.

283
00:09:46,410 --> 00:09:48,577
There are rice fields and farms here.

284
00:09:49,489 --> 00:09:50,757
(Eating snacks to keep her mouth shut)

285
00:09:50,758 --> 00:09:53,125
Maybe it's better if you don't talk.

286
00:09:53,126 --> 00:09:55,060
Just keep eating.

287
00:09:55,362 --> 00:09:56,362
Okay?

288
00:09:56,363 --> 00:09:57,530
Good.

289
00:09:57,531 --> 00:09:58,864
Lee Sian from "Single's Inferno."

290
00:09:58,865 --> 00:10:01,534
(Laughing)

291
00:10:02,402 --> 00:10:05,171
Lee Sian is there at the perfect moment.

292
00:10:06,282 --> 00:10:07,262
(Peace sign)

293
00:10:08,635 --> 00:10:11,248
(An Indonesian passenger happens
to take a photo.)

294
00:10:11,862 --> 00:10:13,980
Maybe they know Lee Sian
from "Single's Inferno."

295
00:10:14,389 --> 00:10:16,889
(Silence)

296
00:10:19,929 --> 00:10:21,929
The huge windows make it so beautiful.

297
00:10:22,242 --> 00:10:24,820
(The view outside is a perk
of train travel.)

298
00:10:25,091 --> 00:10:27,427
Why does it already feel like a jungle?

299
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:29,429
There are palm trees.

300
00:10:29,882 --> 00:10:31,030
The view is beautiful.

301
00:10:31,031 --> 00:10:34,191
It feels different from Bangkok.

302
00:10:34,192 --> 00:10:35,168
Exactly.

303
00:10:35,169 --> 00:10:37,396
There aren't any buildings.

304
00:10:37,397 --> 00:10:39,839
- The sky is wide open.
- Isn't this a jungle?

305
00:10:40,373 --> 00:10:41,508
The world is so big.

306
00:10:42,529 --> 00:10:43,676
The world really is huge.

307
00:10:43,916 --> 00:10:46,646
It has so many different places.

308
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:49,895
(What other places await them
in Indonesia?)

309
00:10:49,988 --> 00:10:52,968
What are we doing in Medan?
What are we doing there?

310
00:10:53,101 --> 00:10:54,154
(We have to eat.)

311
00:10:54,155 --> 00:10:55,955
We'll eat as soon as we reach Medan.

312
00:10:56,035 --> 00:10:58,258
What food is Indonesia known for?

313
00:10:58,508 --> 00:10:59,726
Here's one.

314
00:11:00,927 --> 00:11:03,263
There's something called Sop Sumsum.

315
00:11:03,328 --> 00:11:04,297
Sumsum?

316
00:11:04,474 --> 00:11:08,535
They say you put a straw in the marrow
and drink it.

317
00:11:09,628 --> 00:11:10,521
It's nourishing.

318
00:11:11,048 --> 00:11:12,741
Put it into the marrow?

319
00:11:12,742 --> 00:11:14,240
That feels like "Attack on Titan."

320
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:15,870
It's like galbitang.

321
00:11:15,871 --> 00:11:16,910
- Oh, galbitang.
- I see.

322
00:11:16,911 --> 00:11:18,417
That sounds like it'd be good.

323
00:11:18,418 --> 00:11:19,512
I seriously love that.

324
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:20,680
Galbitang club.

325
00:11:20,707 --> 00:11:22,916
And there's a juice.

326
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:24,751
It's called Jus Martabe.

327
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,627
They say it's rich in antioxidants.

328
00:11:27,628 --> 00:11:30,423
I've aged so fast over the past week.

329
00:11:30,632 --> 00:11:32,759
Worn out, to be exact.

330
00:11:32,912 --> 00:11:35,695
This looks good. I really want to try it.

331
00:11:36,296 --> 00:11:39,032
- It's like galbitang.
- Yes.

332
00:11:39,586 --> 00:11:41,935
I got a text.

333
00:11:42,241 --> 00:11:46,206
- What does it say?
- I got a text.

334
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:51,711
A travel budget of 117.5 dollars
per person has been deposited.

335
00:11:51,712 --> 00:11:54,099
It seems they suddenly cut it in half.

336
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,182
We had 230 dollars before.

337
00:11:56,183 --> 00:11:58,183
They applied the burger index...

338
00:11:58,184 --> 00:12:00,564
because things are cheaper here.

339
00:12:00,565 --> 00:12:02,088
- Still.
- What's the burger index?

340
00:12:02,089 --> 00:12:05,258
- What was that burger index from before?
- The McDonald's burger index.

341
00:12:05,259 --> 00:12:07,856
- But still.
- That one.

342
00:12:08,036 --> 00:12:10,663
Isn't 110 dollars too little?

343
00:12:10,664 --> 00:12:13,333
The prices must be lower than in Bangkok.

344
00:12:14,315 --> 00:12:16,768
But they cut it too drastically.

345
00:12:17,215 --> 00:12:18,204
Too drastic!

346
00:12:19,688 --> 00:12:22,342
Let's discuss this again later.

347
00:12:22,343 --> 00:12:25,249
Since we're on the train,
let's talk after we get off.

348
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:27,380
I don't want us to just accept it.

349
00:12:27,569 --> 00:12:30,483
Won Ji, how much was the train ticket?

350
00:12:30,616 --> 00:12:33,253
We need to get a sense of local prices.

351
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:35,488
About 4 dollars per person.

352
00:12:35,489 --> 00:12:36,589
- This?
- Yes.

353
00:12:36,708 --> 00:12:38,048
- It's 4 dollars and 20 cents?
- Yes.

354
00:12:38,148 --> 00:12:40,193
Isn't that a great price for this quality?

355
00:12:40,295 --> 00:12:42,595
It really is cheap.

356
00:12:43,228 --> 00:12:44,397
I have nothing to say.

357
00:12:44,731 --> 00:12:45,922
It's so cheap that I'm speechless.

358
00:12:45,955 --> 00:12:47,300
We can make it work.

359
00:12:47,301 --> 00:12:49,301
- We'll have to lower our standards.
- It is cheap.

360
00:12:49,769 --> 00:12:51,804
And we don't have much to spend money on.

361
00:12:51,873 --> 00:12:53,673
We're going into the jungle.

362
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:56,676
There's nowhere to spend money.

363
00:12:56,677 --> 00:12:57,940
(Nothing to buy in the jungle)

364
00:12:58,993 --> 00:13:01,720
(Looking around)

365
00:13:02,106 --> 00:13:04,533
(Waving)

366
00:13:05,606 --> 00:13:08,366
(They spot an adorable baby.)

367
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:11,324
- The baby's cute.
- Hello.

368
00:13:12,581 --> 00:13:13,860
So cute.

369
00:13:14,887 --> 00:13:16,814
(Giggles)

370
00:13:16,914 --> 00:13:18,331
(Playing with the baby)

371
00:13:19,668 --> 00:13:21,901
Let's go.

372
00:13:21,902 --> 00:13:23,134
(Dark mage Gabee controls the baby.)

373
00:13:25,128 --> 00:13:26,372
- Did you say "Hye Rim?"
- What was that?

374
00:13:26,641 --> 00:13:28,408
Did she say "Hye Rim?"

375
00:13:28,409 --> 00:13:29,709
(Did she just say my name?)

376
00:13:29,710 --> 00:13:30,777
That's me.

377
00:13:30,778 --> 00:13:31,811
She said Hye Rim.

378
00:13:32,484 --> 00:13:34,484
She put it on her head.

379
00:13:38,771 --> 00:13:40,584
(Staring)

380
00:13:42,998 --> 00:13:44,998
(Scared)

381
00:13:44,999 --> 00:13:46,159
The baby must be scared.

382
00:13:46,418 --> 00:13:47,393
You try it.

383
00:13:50,525 --> 00:13:52,632
That's scary even for me.

384
00:13:55,085 --> 00:14:00,372
(Amazingly, the baby didn't cry.)

385
00:14:00,478 --> 00:14:04,344
I don't think Sian is
quite in her right mind.

386
00:14:04,565 --> 00:14:06,279
That's why I think she's fun.

387
00:14:07,261 --> 00:14:08,314
I'm rooting for her.

388
00:14:10,174 --> 00:14:13,474
(Go, Lee Sian!)

389
00:14:14,887 --> 00:14:16,134
We'll arrive around five.

390
00:14:16,135 --> 00:14:17,290
Where's your wallpaper from?

391
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:18,257
The Himalayas.

392
00:14:18,258 --> 00:14:20,258
A woman who's been to the Himalayas!

393
00:14:20,277 --> 00:14:23,317
(The woman who's been to the Himalayas
returns after a long absence.)

394
00:14:23,830 --> 00:14:26,050
A woman who's been to the Himalayas!

395
00:14:26,051 --> 00:14:26,691
(Staring)

396
00:14:28,497 --> 00:14:30,283
(Avoiding her gaze)

397
00:14:30,463 --> 00:14:33,673
The woman who climbed the Himalayas!

398
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:37,250
The woman who climbed the Himalayas!

399
00:14:37,930 --> 00:14:39,537
(Wheezing)

400
00:14:40,657 --> 00:14:42,415
At least my voice sounded similar.

401
00:14:43,616 --> 00:14:45,385
It did sound similar.

402
00:14:45,685 --> 00:14:49,355
She's totally Won Ji, the woman
who climbed the Himalayas.

403
00:14:50,178 --> 00:14:51,811
True, true!

404
00:14:51,812 --> 00:14:53,812
That girl, Won Ji.

405
00:14:53,813 --> 00:14:55,420
That woman, Won Ji.

406
00:14:56,162 --> 00:14:57,296
(A weak replication)

407
00:14:59,166 --> 00:15:00,900
That woman, Won Ji.

408
00:15:00,901 --> 00:15:02,907
(Good luck, Won Ji!)

409
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,303
This is hard.

410
00:15:04,304 --> 00:15:05,371
Bedtime.

411
00:15:07,293 --> 00:15:09,530
Let's all go to sleep now.

412
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,324
(Her true feelings slip out.)

413
00:15:12,524 --> 00:15:14,147
Why won't anyone go to sleep?

414
00:15:14,497 --> 00:15:15,548
Let's sleep.

415
00:15:16,983 --> 00:15:19,685
The houses look more densely packed now.

416
00:15:20,253 --> 00:15:21,788
It's a real city now.

417
00:15:21,969 --> 00:15:25,269
(The scenery has transformed into a city.)

418
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:27,059
Now we can see cafes and things.

419
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:29,160
There are really tall buildings.

420
00:15:29,595 --> 00:15:31,297
It's my first time in Medan.

421
00:15:32,075 --> 00:15:34,200
There are definitely lots
of big buildings now.

422
00:15:37,715 --> 00:15:39,672
(Gridlocked traffic)

423
00:15:39,673 --> 00:15:43,215
They said driving would take two hours.

424
00:15:43,216 --> 00:15:45,611
- Indonesia has terrible traffic.
- Yes.

425
00:15:45,682 --> 00:15:47,213
(Medan Station announcement)

426
00:15:47,647 --> 00:15:49,255
It's a quarter to five now.

427
00:15:50,375 --> 00:15:51,589
This is Medan Station.

428
00:15:51,955 --> 00:15:54,909
We're at the last stop.

429
00:15:54,910 --> 00:15:58,618
- We're here.
- Medan.

430
00:15:59,192 --> 00:16:00,393
- Bye.
- Have a happy holiday!

431
00:16:00,572 --> 00:16:01,627
Happy holiday!

432
00:16:01,665 --> 00:16:03,396
(One last goodbye to the baby)

433
00:16:04,063 --> 00:16:07,733
I'll take this and get off first.

434
00:16:07,809 --> 00:16:09,135
Escape.

435
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:14,469
They've got some big buildings here.

436
00:16:14,496 --> 00:16:17,944
There's a supermarket. We can buy things.

437
00:16:18,189 --> 00:16:20,480
This must be the main area.

438
00:16:21,314 --> 00:16:23,049
This is definitely a city, everyone.

439
00:16:23,583 --> 00:16:25,751
Where was our lodging again?

440
00:16:25,752 --> 00:16:28,988
Do we need a taxi to get there?

441
00:16:29,312 --> 00:16:30,490
This must be it.

442
00:16:31,306 --> 00:16:33,692
We can just show them this address, right?

443
00:16:33,693 --> 00:16:34,393
Yes.

444
00:16:35,426 --> 00:16:36,896
- Taxi?
- Yes.

445
00:16:37,092 --> 00:16:38,698
We are four people.

446
00:16:39,198 --> 00:16:40,432
Do you know here?

447
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:41,252
(Lodging address)

448
00:16:41,325 --> 00:16:41,934
Okay.

449
00:16:41,935 --> 00:16:42,902
- Okay.
- Okay?

450
00:16:42,972 --> 00:16:43,970
How much is it?

451
00:16:44,679 --> 00:16:46,481
(Nervous)

452
00:16:47,168 --> 00:16:48,328
It's a metered taxi.

453
00:16:48,548 --> 00:16:49,635
Metered.

454
00:16:49,636 --> 00:16:51,944
- It's metered. Great.
- Great.

455
00:16:52,035 --> 00:16:54,213
I like metered taxis.

456
00:16:54,375 --> 00:16:55,915
(A sudden confession)

457
00:16:56,621 --> 00:16:57,750
One suitcase.

458
00:16:57,853 --> 00:16:58,851
One suitcase?

459
00:16:58,913 --> 00:16:59,919
Only one.

460
00:17:01,539 --> 00:17:04,879
(Their precious suitcase is loaded first.)

461
00:17:05,626 --> 00:17:07,660
(Getting into the taxi)

462
00:17:07,661 --> 00:17:09,228
Hello.

463
00:17:09,714 --> 00:17:12,465
The base fare is 8,000 rupiah.

464
00:17:12,466 --> 00:17:16,002
I'll check the exchange rate.

465
00:17:16,594 --> 00:17:19,705
I think 10,000 rupiah is about 80 cents.

466
00:17:19,934 --> 00:17:20,973
I think 10,000 rupiah is 80 cents.

467
00:17:20,974 --> 00:17:22,341
We got a great exchange rate.

468
00:17:22,448 --> 00:17:23,609
You said 10,000 rupiah is 80 cents?

469
00:17:23,721 --> 00:17:28,448
Wait, the base fare is 8,000 rupiah
on the meter.

470
00:17:28,449 --> 00:17:30,816
That's about 68 cents.

471
00:17:30,994 --> 00:17:32,919
Then it's extremely cheap, right?

472
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,754
The base fare is roughly 50 cents.

473
00:17:35,096 --> 00:17:37,663
(The taxi slowly leaves the station.)

474
00:17:37,664 --> 00:17:38,824
You can move back a little.

475
00:17:38,943 --> 00:17:40,793
Are we going to our lodging?

476
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:41,761
- Our lodging.
- Yes.

477
00:17:41,831 --> 00:17:43,462
How long will it take?

478
00:17:43,524 --> 00:17:46,399
- About 20 minutes.
- Right.

479
00:17:46,917 --> 00:17:49,769
Didn't Bangkok feel hotter?

480
00:17:49,957 --> 00:17:52,024
- Right? I think so too.
- Why is that?

481
00:17:52,090 --> 00:17:53,172
Because it's afternoon?

482
00:17:53,309 --> 00:17:55,564
But it was hot in the afternoon too.

483
00:17:55,565 --> 00:18:00,212
Right. Bangkok and Chiang Mai were so hot
around 4 or 5 p.m. The sun was blazing.

484
00:18:00,268 --> 00:18:02,882
Does all the rain cool things down?

485
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:05,115
Maybe because the ground is damp.

486
00:18:05,116 --> 00:18:06,886
It must cool everything right down.

487
00:18:07,055 --> 00:18:10,122
- To me, it feels much cooler.
- It's cooler here.

488
00:18:10,321 --> 00:18:11,724
Maybe because it's so windy?

489
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:15,288
The traffic is definitely bad here.

490
00:18:15,289 --> 00:18:16,128
Totally.

491
00:18:16,562 --> 00:18:19,265
That must be why people ride motorcycles.

492
00:18:19,632 --> 00:18:22,535
But it's really half cars,
half motorcycles.

493
00:18:22,935 --> 00:18:24,270
They're like bicycles here.

494
00:18:25,871 --> 00:18:28,207
It must feel so freeing on a motorcycle.

495
00:18:29,091 --> 00:18:31,885
(They spend quite a while on the road.)

496
00:18:32,131 --> 00:18:33,479
- Hello.
- Yes.

497
00:18:33,505 --> 00:18:35,114
Can you speak English?

498
00:18:35,198 --> 00:18:36,349
A little bit.

499
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:37,530
A little bit?

500
00:18:38,436 --> 00:18:41,153
Can you recommend...

501
00:18:41,554 --> 00:18:42,922
Indonesian food?

502
00:18:43,123 --> 00:18:44,357
- Yes.
- Indonesian food?

503
00:18:44,423 --> 00:18:46,423
Yes, the best food.

504
00:18:46,630 --> 00:18:47,442
(Thinking)

505
00:18:47,443 --> 00:18:48,294
Soto?

506
00:18:48,416 --> 00:18:50,188
- Soto?
- Soto.

507
00:18:50,189 --> 00:18:51,930
(The unfamiliar dish called Soto)

508
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:53,232
Soto.

509
00:18:53,233 --> 00:18:57,566
(Soto is a traditional Indonesian soup
with regional ingredients and flavors.)

510
00:18:57,893 --> 00:19:00,606
Have you heard of Bukit Lawang?

511
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,641
Yes.

512
00:19:01,746 --> 00:19:03,009
Do you know Bukit Lawang?

513
00:19:03,010 --> 00:19:05,945
Have you been there? We're going tomorrow.

514
00:19:06,406 --> 00:19:09,399
(As they rapidly ask him for advice,)

515
00:19:10,866 --> 00:19:13,219
(they enter a bustling downtown area.)

516
00:19:13,286 --> 00:19:15,721
- Korea.
- A Korean convenience store.

517
00:19:16,096 --> 00:19:17,230
(A K-mart in Medan)

518
00:19:17,231 --> 00:19:18,958
There's a Korean convenience store.

519
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:22,163
Tteokbokki and corn dogs.

520
00:19:22,164 --> 00:19:23,262
Tteokbokki? Where?

521
00:19:24,063 --> 00:19:25,031
Delicious.

522
00:19:25,076 --> 00:19:26,956
- It says Korea.
- What is it?

523
00:19:27,003 --> 00:19:30,196
Indonesians seem to love Korean culture.

524
00:19:30,197 --> 00:19:31,671
I think they really do.

525
00:19:32,110 --> 00:19:33,916
There's a place called Kimchi Booth.

526
00:19:33,917 --> 00:19:35,107
- Let's go there.
- Okay.

527
00:19:35,108 --> 00:19:36,308
- Looks good.
- Let's go.

528
00:19:36,609 --> 00:19:38,077
But it's a photo booth.

529
00:19:38,444 --> 00:19:39,178
(What?)

530
00:19:39,179 --> 00:19:40,279
Kimchi Booth.

531
00:19:40,806 --> 00:19:42,506
Proof of the Korean Wave.

532
00:19:42,507 --> 00:19:46,160
I thought it was a restaurant
that served kimchi dishes.

533
00:19:46,161 --> 00:19:47,653
Don't you want kimchi fried rice?

534
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:50,667
Who invented kimchi? They're incredible.

535
00:19:51,824 --> 00:19:53,659
Our ancestors.

536
00:19:53,742 --> 00:19:55,928
Our ancestors were legendary foodies.

537
00:19:55,955 --> 00:19:57,296
She called them real foodies.

538
00:19:58,422 --> 00:20:01,214
You sounded so millennial, no, so Gen Z.

539
00:20:01,215 --> 00:20:02,715
That was such a Gen Z moment.

540
00:20:02,716 --> 00:20:03,950
Our ancestors were foodie...

541
00:20:03,951 --> 00:20:05,118
Legends.

542
00:20:05,386 --> 00:20:07,319
Those three words...

543
00:20:07,621 --> 00:20:11,123
Ancestors, foodie, legends.

544
00:20:11,525 --> 00:20:13,926
(An unexpected word combination)

545
00:20:14,261 --> 00:20:16,829
I want to speak Gen Z.

546
00:20:17,564 --> 00:20:20,166
Remember how...

547
00:20:20,234 --> 00:20:23,436
our moms would try to talk like us,
and it would sound funny?

548
00:20:23,437 --> 00:20:24,371
Wouldn't it be the same?

549
00:20:24,372 --> 00:20:26,873
(Kind of like this)

550
00:20:27,474 --> 00:20:29,775
My mom speaks like this, though.

551
00:20:29,776 --> 00:20:30,709
Really?

552
00:20:32,146 --> 00:20:33,046
That's unexpected.

553
00:20:33,881 --> 00:20:37,016
Does your mother also say
your ancestors were legends?

554
00:20:37,251 --> 00:20:38,117
Yes.

555
00:20:38,118 --> 00:20:40,486
- Foodies.
- She does pretty often.

556
00:20:40,487 --> 00:20:41,654
Gosh.

557
00:20:41,855 --> 00:20:43,321
It must be nice to click with your mom.

558
00:20:43,322 --> 00:20:45,858
I'll introduce her to you.

559
00:20:45,859 --> 00:20:46,859
You'll introduce your mother to us?

560
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:47,912
(Tracing the roots of Gen Z energy)

561
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:51,497
- When was your mother born?
- In 1975.

562
00:20:52,433 --> 00:20:53,600
This must be the place.

563
00:20:55,736 --> 00:20:57,236
We're here.

564
00:20:57,304 --> 00:21:00,072
This looks like a hotel.

565
00:21:00,073 --> 00:21:01,674
This is nice.

566
00:21:01,675 --> 00:21:02,842
(Arriving at their sleek Medan stay)

567
00:21:02,843 --> 00:21:03,909
We're here!

568
00:21:03,910 --> 00:21:05,845
We're here.

569
00:21:05,846 --> 00:21:07,480
(Excitedly getting out of the taxi)

570
00:21:07,481 --> 00:21:09,215
Wow.

571
00:21:09,216 --> 00:21:10,149
Okay.

572
00:21:10,150 --> 00:21:12,585
- Bye-bye.
- Thank you!

573
00:21:12,586 --> 00:21:14,887
Thank you.

574
00:21:14,888 --> 00:21:17,189
Let's go to the 1st floor
and tell them our names,

575
00:21:17,190 --> 00:21:18,658
so they can help us check in.

576
00:21:18,659 --> 00:21:20,493
All right.

577
00:21:21,762 --> 00:21:23,863
Hello, can I check in now?

578
00:21:23,864 --> 00:21:25,098
Oh, okay.

579
00:21:25,899 --> 00:21:27,600
We booked on Airbnb.

580
00:21:27,868 --> 00:21:29,368
(Showing her the reservation)

581
00:21:29,369 --> 00:21:30,770
Thank you.

582
00:21:31,404 --> 00:21:33,706
This is your card and key.

583
00:21:33,707 --> 00:21:37,043
Room 1H is on the 1st floor.

584
00:21:37,044 --> 00:21:39,445
Okay, thank you so much.

585
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:40,813
Let's go.

586
00:21:40,814 --> 00:21:42,482
(Taking the elevator up)

587
00:21:42,883 --> 00:21:45,818
Let's all squeeze in.

588
00:21:46,286 --> 00:21:49,088
(From the lobby to the 1st floor)

589
00:21:49,089 --> 00:21:51,156
We're here.

590
00:21:51,157 --> 00:21:53,292
Let me give you your tickets.

591
00:21:54,094 --> 00:21:55,460
(Opening)

592
00:21:57,965 --> 00:22:00,099
- This is nice.
- This is great!

593
00:22:00,434 --> 00:22:02,769
- This is awesome.
- This is the best!

594
00:22:02,770 --> 00:22:04,070
(A cozy, modern living room)

595
00:22:04,071 --> 00:22:06,105
How about the rooms? There are two.

596
00:22:06,106 --> 00:22:07,640
(Two large bedrooms
to soothe travel fatigue)

597
00:22:07,641 --> 00:22:09,375
These are the bedrooms.

598
00:22:09,943 --> 00:22:11,510
This is pretty cozy.

599
00:22:11,745 --> 00:22:14,013
There's a terrace here too.

600
00:22:14,114 --> 00:22:15,014
Gosh!

601
00:22:15,015 --> 00:22:17,049
A terrace too?

602
00:22:17,050 --> 00:22:18,718
This is nice.

603
00:22:18,719 --> 00:22:21,153
(A refreshing terrace)

604
00:22:21,622 --> 00:22:24,757
We have a washing machine, too.
I'm touched.

605
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:29,529
We have a washing machine!

606
00:22:29,530 --> 00:22:30,630
This is so nice!

607
00:22:30,631 --> 00:22:33,566
- Home, sweet home.
- Shame we're staying only one night.

608
00:22:33,567 --> 00:22:34,834
(A pleasant start to their Indonesia trip)

609
00:22:35,235 --> 00:22:36,769
Now, who got you this place?

610
00:22:37,171 --> 00:22:39,172
Won Ji!

611
00:22:39,173 --> 00:22:41,174
Let's give a shout-out to Won Ji!

612
00:22:41,175 --> 00:22:42,995
Won Ji, you're a genius!

613
00:22:42,996 --> 00:22:45,645
(Taking in the shout-outs)

614
00:22:45,646 --> 00:22:48,681
She might be hungry,

615
00:22:48,682 --> 00:22:50,850
but she can still find a great place.

616
00:22:51,652 --> 00:22:52,719
Period.

617
00:22:53,153 --> 00:22:55,154
Thank you for your enthusiasm.

618
00:22:55,422 --> 00:22:57,823
Since we've checked in,

619
00:22:57,824 --> 00:22:58,991
why don't we try Sop Sumsum...

620
00:22:58,992 --> 00:23:01,093
to refill our energy?

621
00:23:01,094 --> 00:23:02,995
I heard Koreans love it.

622
00:23:02,996 --> 00:23:04,830
- Okay.
- Let's go.

623
00:23:04,831 --> 00:23:06,031
Okay, let's go.

624
00:23:06,032 --> 00:23:09,034
Let's go refill our energy!

625
00:23:10,204 --> 00:23:12,539
- I'm so excited.
- Gosh.

626
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:14,742
- Everyone.
- Yes?

627
00:23:14,743 --> 00:23:16,543
So I saw...

628
00:23:17,344 --> 00:23:19,245
that over there.

629
00:23:19,379 --> 00:23:22,014
It's called a bentor.

630
00:23:22,816 --> 00:23:24,917
(Bentor: unique transportation
in northern Sumatra in Indonesia...)

631
00:23:24,918 --> 00:23:28,187
(that combines rickshaw and motorcycle.)

632
00:23:28,188 --> 00:23:30,156
I want to ride a bentor.

633
00:23:30,157 --> 00:23:31,857
- Let's try the bentor.
- I'd love to.

634
00:23:31,858 --> 00:23:33,092
It will only take 8 minutes.

635
00:23:33,093 --> 00:23:33,993
Nice.

636
00:23:33,994 --> 00:23:36,062
Let's pick teams.

637
00:23:36,063 --> 00:23:36,997
Let's do palms up, palms down then.

638
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:38,564
- Palms up, palms down!
- Palms up, palms down!

639
00:23:38,565 --> 00:23:39,699
Bummer.

640
00:23:39,700 --> 00:23:41,100
(Trying again)

641
00:23:41,582 --> 00:23:43,616
(Harimu, Sian: palms,
Gabee, Won Ji: back of hand)

642
00:23:43,937 --> 00:23:46,105
(Secret Santa buddies get together.)

643
00:23:46,106 --> 00:23:48,574
- Let's go.
- Let's go bargain.

644
00:23:49,076 --> 00:23:50,544
So you have to bargain here, too.

645
00:23:50,545 --> 00:23:52,512
Hello! Excuse me.
A motorcycle!

646
00:23:53,013 --> 00:23:54,013
Do you know this place?

647
00:23:54,014 --> 00:23:55,214
(Sharing the restaurant location first)

648
00:23:55,215 --> 00:23:55,982
Here.

649
00:23:56,116 --> 00:23:57,917
It's 8 minutes? How about 5 minutes?

650
00:23:58,619 --> 00:24:00,520
(Knocking off 3 minutes)

651
00:24:00,888 --> 00:24:02,222
How much is it?

652
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:05,224
You're the best, Won Ji! Let's bargain!

653
00:24:06,326 --> 00:24:09,194
(Cheering on Won Ji's bargain)

654
00:24:09,296 --> 00:24:10,897
- What?
- How much?

655
00:24:10,898 --> 00:24:11,931
How much?

656
00:24:12,300 --> 00:24:14,000
(Something's not going well)

657
00:24:14,534 --> 00:24:16,635
How much is the fare?

658
00:24:17,404 --> 00:24:18,804
(English communication not working)

659
00:24:19,740 --> 00:24:21,274
For two people.

660
00:24:21,508 --> 00:24:22,675
How much is it, Won Ji?

661
00:24:22,676 --> 00:24:23,642
How much is the fare?

662
00:24:24,378 --> 00:24:25,511
How much is it?

663
00:24:25,913 --> 00:24:26,813
(Get on first.)

664
00:24:27,015 --> 00:24:28,681
Should we get on first?

665
00:24:29,283 --> 00:24:31,684
- Is this okay?
- Let's get on first and go.

666
00:24:32,019 --> 00:24:32,986
See you later!

667
00:24:32,987 --> 00:24:35,788
(They set out in two different bentors.)

668
00:24:36,290 --> 00:24:38,258
This is so cool.

669
00:24:39,393 --> 00:24:41,262
The rider is...

670
00:24:41,263 --> 00:24:42,862
next to us instead of the front.

671
00:24:42,863 --> 00:24:44,464
We're going side by side.

672
00:24:45,366 --> 00:24:46,031
Let's go!

673
00:24:46,032 --> 00:24:47,166
Let's go!

674
00:24:48,368 --> 00:24:50,769
Let's go! See you later!

675
00:24:51,605 --> 00:24:52,738
Finally, we're eating.

676
00:24:52,739 --> 00:24:54,674
We're going to eat.

677
00:24:57,744 --> 00:25:00,479
The weather's pretty cool.
Is it because it's the rainy season?

678
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:01,414
Right.

679
00:25:01,415 --> 00:25:03,082
I think it's the rainy season.

680
00:25:03,083 --> 00:25:04,650
The rain must have a cooling effect.

681
00:25:05,152 --> 00:25:07,487
It's such a relief
because I was worried it might be hot.

682
00:25:07,488 --> 00:25:09,522
This is cooler than Thailand.

683
00:25:10,190 --> 00:25:11,657
The jungle might not be so bad.

684
00:25:11,658 --> 00:25:12,491
Right.

685
00:25:12,927 --> 00:25:14,994
It's so nice and cool.

686
00:25:15,529 --> 00:25:16,996
Is this downtown?

687
00:25:17,464 --> 00:25:18,597
This looks like...

688
00:25:19,066 --> 00:25:20,466
a busy street.

689
00:25:20,467 --> 00:25:21,840
This is nice.

690
00:25:21,841 --> 00:25:22,835
(The bentor ventures downtown.)

691
00:25:22,936 --> 00:25:24,270
(Exclaiming)

692
00:25:24,538 --> 00:25:26,506
It's been a while since we came
somewhere this busy.

693
00:25:26,507 --> 00:25:27,306
Right.

694
00:25:27,774 --> 00:25:29,141
This is the first time.

695
00:25:29,142 --> 00:25:31,443
There are so many motorcycles here.

696
00:25:37,884 --> 00:25:40,786
We got on without bargaining, right?

697
00:25:40,787 --> 00:25:41,653
Right.

698
00:25:41,654 --> 00:25:43,188
I'm going to look up the average fare.

699
00:25:43,189 --> 00:25:45,057
That sounds like a good idea.

700
00:25:45,792 --> 00:25:47,626
Tourist...

701
00:25:47,627 --> 00:25:48,627
(Searching)

702
00:25:48,628 --> 00:25:53,599
It's 30,000 rupiah for foreigners.

703
00:25:53,701 --> 00:25:56,502
- Let's pay 30,000 rupiah each.
- Sounds good.

704
00:25:56,503 --> 00:25:57,636
Right, let's be generous.

705
00:25:57,704 --> 00:25:59,171
(Glancing)

706
00:25:59,172 --> 00:26:00,005
This must be the place.

707
00:26:00,540 --> 00:26:04,176
Sop Sumsum. This is the place.

708
00:26:04,177 --> 00:26:05,311
We're here.

709
00:26:05,445 --> 00:26:06,378
Okay.

710
00:26:06,379 --> 00:26:08,514
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

711
00:26:08,515 --> 00:26:09,848
It smells good.

712
00:26:10,083 --> 00:26:11,050
We're here.

713
00:26:11,284 --> 00:26:12,184
Excuse me.

714
00:26:12,819 --> 00:26:14,486
Excuse me.

715
00:26:14,855 --> 00:26:15,688
How about 30,000 rupiah.

716
00:26:16,957 --> 00:26:18,658
(Making the initial offer)

717
00:26:18,992 --> 00:26:19,862
(Using gestures and the calculator)

718
00:26:19,863 --> 00:26:21,927
For this one and that one.

719
00:26:22,295 --> 00:26:24,496
(Confirming with the other driver)

720
00:26:24,497 --> 00:26:25,230
How about 30,000.

721
00:26:25,231 --> 00:26:26,732
(Set on 30,000.)

722
00:26:26,733 --> 00:26:27,532
Okay?

723
00:26:27,533 --> 00:26:29,201
That's 30,000 each.

724
00:26:29,202 --> 00:26:30,803
(Deal accepted)

725
00:26:30,804 --> 00:26:32,671
It's just 2 dollars.

726
00:26:32,672 --> 00:26:34,172
(Getting used to bargaining)

727
00:26:34,307 --> 00:26:36,675
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

728
00:26:36,676 --> 00:26:39,745
Okay, let's eat.

729
00:26:39,746 --> 00:26:40,679
(Excited.)

730
00:26:41,481 --> 00:26:43,449
- It smells so nice.
- It's going to be delicious.

731
00:26:43,516 --> 00:26:45,118
It smells just like beef rib soup.

732
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:47,319
Hello.

733
00:26:47,421 --> 00:26:49,555
- The smell is killer.
- This is going to be good.

734
00:26:49,956 --> 00:26:52,057
Should we sit here?

735
00:26:52,058 --> 00:26:52,925
(Finding seats first)

736
00:26:52,926 --> 00:26:55,027
They have a lot on the menu.

737
00:26:55,328 --> 00:26:58,664
I heard you have to try this
when you're here.

738
00:26:58,833 --> 00:27:00,766
There's really a straw in the bone.

739
00:27:00,767 --> 00:27:01,801
Right.

740
00:27:01,802 --> 00:27:03,135
Also, I feel like...

741
00:27:03,136 --> 00:27:05,671
we need to recharge
since our blood sugar is low.

742
00:27:06,339 --> 00:27:07,372
Seriously.

743
00:27:08,041 --> 00:27:11,243
What was the name? Let's see.

744
00:27:11,479 --> 00:27:12,845
This looks like their signature menu.

745
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:15,014
Jus Martabe.

746
00:27:15,649 --> 00:27:16,515
Here it is.

747
00:27:17,084 --> 00:27:18,317
Let's order four of these.

748
00:27:18,419 --> 00:27:20,986
- Don't we need rice too?
- Let's ask.

749
00:27:21,655 --> 00:27:22,454
We're ready to order.

750
00:27:22,455 --> 00:27:23,989
(Ordering shyly)

751
00:27:23,990 --> 00:27:25,624
Four Sop Sumsum.

752
00:27:26,026 --> 00:27:28,394
Four rice.

753
00:27:28,395 --> 00:27:29,228
Okay.

754
00:27:29,229 --> 00:27:31,430
Four Jus Martabe.

755
00:27:31,431 --> 00:27:32,832
Okay.

756
00:27:32,833 --> 00:27:33,733
Thank you.

757
00:27:33,734 --> 00:27:35,134
I'm so excited about the juice.

758
00:27:35,135 --> 00:27:36,035
It looks so good.

759
00:27:36,570 --> 00:27:38,304
It looks energizing.

760
00:27:38,405 --> 00:27:40,239
It's actually an energy-boosting dish.

761
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:42,575
Let's eat this and get charged up...

762
00:27:42,876 --> 00:27:44,210
to go to the jungle tomorrow.

763
00:27:44,211 --> 00:27:46,679
I'm so hungry. I need food now.

764
00:27:47,180 --> 00:27:48,480
I'm hungry.

765
00:27:48,481 --> 00:27:49,613
- I need food now.
- I need food now.

766
00:27:49,614 --> 00:27:51,750
(A perfect pair)

767
00:27:51,918 --> 00:27:52,651
I need food now.

768
00:27:52,652 --> 00:27:54,086
(Shocked)

769
00:27:55,822 --> 00:27:58,424
Wow, it looks amazing.

770
00:27:58,425 --> 00:27:59,792
It looks delicious.

771
00:27:59,793 --> 00:28:01,160
It's much bigger than I thought.

772
00:28:03,397 --> 00:28:05,063
I've never seen anything like this.

773
00:28:08,969 --> 00:28:10,436
Look at the straw!

774
00:28:10,770 --> 00:28:11,837
What's all this?

775
00:28:11,838 --> 00:28:13,372
Let's take a photo.

776
00:28:13,373 --> 00:28:14,639
(Sop Sumsum: bone marrow soup)

777
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,341
Is the bone marrow inside?

778
00:28:16,342 --> 00:28:17,175
I think so.

779
00:28:17,176 --> 00:28:19,411
- This is so cool.
- It looks delicious.

780
00:28:19,646 --> 00:28:20,512
Let's look inside.

781
00:28:20,513 --> 00:28:22,147
(Shocked)

782
00:28:22,148 --> 00:28:23,849
You can see the white bone marrow inside.

783
00:28:23,850 --> 00:28:25,584
(Full of marrow)

784
00:28:25,752 --> 00:28:27,887
Can you see the bone marrow inside?

785
00:28:28,455 --> 00:28:30,289
(Taking a photo before digging in)

786
00:28:31,958 --> 00:28:32,925
Okay.

787
00:28:33,093 --> 00:28:33,993
Wow.

788
00:28:34,162 --> 00:28:36,395
- Should we dig in?
- This is insane.

789
00:28:36,730 --> 00:28:38,330
I'm going to try the broth first.

790
00:28:38,331 --> 00:28:41,200
(Trying the broth first)

791
00:28:41,201 --> 00:28:42,234
Wow.

792
00:28:42,802 --> 00:28:43,902
(One more spoonful)

793
00:28:45,172 --> 00:28:46,506
It's just like beef rib soup.

794
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:48,874
Time to mix it with rice.

795
00:28:49,075 --> 00:28:49,941
It's good.

796
00:28:50,611 --> 00:28:51,343
Nice.

797
00:28:52,179 --> 00:28:55,547
It's like a salty, seasoned beef rib soup.

798
00:28:57,317 --> 00:28:58,417
Goodness.

799
00:28:58,418 --> 00:28:59,351
Time to mix it with rice.

800
00:28:59,953 --> 00:29:01,420
It's a bit salty.

801
00:29:02,122 --> 00:29:03,389
Indonesia is a tropical country.

802
00:29:03,390 --> 00:29:04,381
- So it's heavily seasoned.
- Right.

803
00:29:04,382 --> 00:29:05,958
This is great. I love this.

804
00:29:05,959 --> 00:29:07,093
I love this kind of food.

805
00:29:08,695 --> 00:29:09,662
It's the tropical weather.

806
00:29:09,663 --> 00:29:10,763
Yum!

807
00:29:11,030 --> 00:29:13,398
I want some glass noodles with it.

808
00:29:13,600 --> 00:29:15,200
That's our foodie.

809
00:29:15,836 --> 00:29:17,670
I can see why Koreans like it.

810
00:29:17,671 --> 00:29:19,972
(Perfect for the Korean palate)

811
00:29:20,073 --> 00:29:21,774
I'm going to try the bone marrow.

812
00:29:22,909 --> 00:29:24,643
(Trying the bone marrow now.)

813
00:29:27,414 --> 00:29:29,348
(Focused)

814
00:29:36,590 --> 00:29:37,957
It's fat.

815
00:29:38,091 --> 00:29:39,725
It's fat, but it's savory...

816
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:41,593
and creamy.

817
00:29:41,594 --> 00:29:43,128
(The bone marrow tastes rich and creamy.)

