00:39:35,407 --> 00:39:37,242
- until the end of the trip.
- It's not even that heavy.

1083
00:39:37,373 --> 00:39:38,543
We have a lot of space left.

1084
00:39:39,177 --> 00:39:41,846
Let's clean up now.

1085
00:39:42,146 --> 00:39:44,146
- Okay!
- Put away the stuff we aren't taking.

1086
00:39:44,482 --> 00:39:46,060
I didn't know we could pack this light.

1087
00:39:46,061 --> 00:39:47,118
It's so possible.

1088
00:39:47,418 --> 00:39:48,633
Done!

1089
00:39:48,853 --> 00:39:50,855
I'm putting this away.

1090
00:39:51,421 --> 00:39:52,357
Bye.

1091
00:39:52,358 --> 00:39:53,625
Let's wash up and go to bed.

1092
00:39:53,626 --> 00:39:55,393
- See you tomorrow.
- Bye.

1093
00:39:55,464 --> 00:39:56,527
Good night!

1094
00:39:57,424 --> 00:40:00,164
(The night deepens in Medan.)

1095
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:03,801
(At dawn when everyone is asleep)

1096
00:40:08,540 --> 00:40:12,343
(Perfect weather for the jungle)

1097
00:40:12,877 --> 00:40:16,313
(Four a.m., at the accommodation)

1098
00:40:16,314 --> 00:40:17,714
(Slide in)

1099
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:23,553
(The suitcases have been confiscated.)

1100
00:40:24,556 --> 00:40:26,657
(Click)

1101
00:40:26,791 --> 00:40:29,459
(1 hour later at 5 a.m., Won Ji wakes up.)

1102
00:40:30,295 --> 00:40:31,762
(Staggering around)

1103
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:34,064
(Looking around)

1104
00:40:35,066 --> 00:40:37,401
(5:10 a.m., everyone wakes up.)

1105
00:40:37,402 --> 00:40:38,335
Where is the suitcase?

1106
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:43,240
Did they take everything out?

1107
00:40:43,509 --> 00:40:45,810
Yes, I think it's all in the bags.

1108
00:40:47,045 --> 00:40:48,612
This is really backpacking.

1109
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:50,414
(On the seventh day,
they accepted reality.)

1110
00:40:51,349 --> 00:40:58,422
(Medan Bus Terminal)

1111
00:40:59,090 --> 00:41:00,257
(Sian handles the backpack.)

1112
00:41:00,258 --> 00:41:01,425
Let's go.

1113
00:41:01,426 --> 00:41:03,860
- Let's go.
- Here we go.

1114
00:41:04,529 --> 00:41:06,530
I'm wearing arm sleeves
for the first time.

1115
00:41:07,599 --> 00:41:09,934
- You really came prepared.
- Of course.

1116
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:13,003
We're at the bus terminal
for Bukit Lawang.

1117
00:41:13,538 --> 00:41:16,240
We can negotiate the price here.

1118
00:41:16,742 --> 00:41:19,175
You've never taken
a bus like this before, right?

1119
00:41:19,176 --> 00:41:20,978
It's my first time negotiating for a bus.

1120
00:41:21,779 --> 00:41:24,914
(A variety of intercity buses)

1121
00:41:24,915 --> 00:41:26,015
There are so many destinations.

1122
00:41:27,652 --> 00:41:29,019
There are so many buses.

1123
00:41:29,020 --> 00:41:31,855
(The lively bus terminal at dawn)

1124
00:41:34,425 --> 00:41:36,726
- Is this it?
- It says Bukit Lawang.

1125
00:41:37,763 --> 00:41:40,230
It's written right here.

1126
00:41:40,231 --> 00:41:42,599
(The destination is written on the bus.)

1127
00:41:42,634 --> 00:41:44,468
The destination is usually written.

1128
00:41:45,236 --> 00:41:46,937
(The Bukit Lawang bus is already packed.)

1129
00:41:46,938 --> 00:41:48,038
Over there.

1130
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:50,507
There are people going to the jungle.

1131
00:41:51,242 --> 00:41:52,142
This is so cool.

1132
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:53,677
(Bukit Lawang)

1133
00:41:53,678 --> 00:41:55,345
- Bukit Lawang?
- Bukit Lawang?

1134
00:41:55,346 --> 00:41:57,982
(So glad to hear that)

1135
00:41:58,316 --> 00:41:59,883
How much is it to Bukit Lawang?

1136
00:42:01,419 --> 00:42:02,919
- It's 80,000 rupiah.
- Eighty thousand?

1137
00:42:03,422 --> 00:42:04,788
- Eighty thousand?
- Yes.

1138
00:42:04,789 --> 00:42:05,689
For one person?

1139
00:42:06,090 --> 00:42:07,090
Yes, for one person.

1140
00:42:07,091 --> 00:42:08,491
That's too expensive.

1141
00:42:08,960 --> 00:42:11,094
(An emphatic shake of the head)

1142
00:42:11,596 --> 00:42:12,629
What about 40,000 rupiah?

1143
00:42:12,630 --> 00:42:14,698
(Let's do half price.)

1144
00:42:14,699 --> 00:42:15,566
Is 40,000 okay?

1145
00:42:15,733 --> 00:42:18,702
(A polite, smiling refusal)

1146
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:21,172
(A smiling counteroffer)

1147
00:42:21,173 --> 00:42:22,673
There are four of us. Is 40,000 okay?

1148
00:42:24,475 --> 00:42:25,875
(How about 50,000?)

1149
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,445
- Fifty thousand per person?
- Yes, for one person.

1150
00:42:28,547 --> 00:42:29,545
Okay.

1151
00:42:29,546 --> 00:42:30,981
(Deal)

1152
00:42:30,982 --> 00:42:33,783
He gave us a discount
from 80,000 to 50,000.

1153
00:42:33,784 --> 00:42:35,752
(They save about ten dollars.)

1154
00:42:35,753 --> 00:42:36,753
Let's go.

1155
00:42:36,754 --> 00:42:38,788
- Great.
- Do we pay now?

1156
00:42:38,789 --> 00:42:39,689
No.

1157
00:42:39,690 --> 00:42:41,625
Do we pay when we get off? Okay.

1158
00:42:41,626 --> 00:42:42,993
We should pay when we get off.

1159
00:42:42,994 --> 00:42:43,927
Let's go.

1160
00:42:44,495 --> 00:42:47,564
(Boarding the bus)

1161
00:42:48,933 --> 00:42:52,369
We're actually going to the jungle.

1162
00:42:52,370 --> 00:42:54,505
(Bukit Lawang, Indonesia)

1163
00:42:57,942 --> 00:42:59,776
(A jungle village surrounded
by tropical rainforest)

1164
00:42:59,777 --> 00:43:03,446
(A home to countless species)

1165
00:43:03,447 --> 00:43:06,116
- Hey.
- My stuff is being taken.

1166
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:07,985
That's mine.

1167
00:43:07,986 --> 00:43:10,253
(The law of survival in the wild)

1168
00:43:10,989 --> 00:43:14,525
(Home of the orangutans)

1169
00:43:15,393 --> 00:43:20,030
(A hidden gem in North Sumatra,
surrounded by nature)

1170
00:43:20,331 --> 00:43:22,499
(Bukit Lawang, the jungle village)

1171
00:43:23,468 --> 00:43:24,601
Here we go.

1172
00:43:25,703 --> 00:43:27,580
(The adventure begins)

1173
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,306
Off to the jungle.

1174
00:43:29,307 --> 00:43:31,474
I'm so excited.

1175
00:43:31,842 --> 00:43:34,145
Me too. I've always wanted to come here.

1176
00:43:34,146 --> 00:43:35,245
Me too.

1177
00:43:35,246 --> 00:43:37,147
It'll take about three hours by car.

1178
00:43:37,148 --> 00:43:38,148
(A three-hour drive to Bukit Lawang)

1179
00:43:38,149 --> 00:43:40,417
I didn't even know
a place like this existed.

1180
00:43:40,418 --> 00:43:41,351
Same.

1181
00:43:42,154 --> 00:43:45,389
I've taken buses like this a lot,

1182
00:43:45,390 --> 00:43:48,592
- but this is your first time, right?
- Totally my first time.

1183
00:43:48,593 --> 00:43:51,328
- I've never taken buses like this.
- It's a local intercity bus.

1184
00:43:51,329 --> 00:43:52,996
It's cooler than I expected.

1185
00:43:52,997 --> 00:43:54,031
It's pretty comfortable.

1186
00:43:54,032 --> 00:43:56,300
- There's air conditioning.
- It's actually quite nice.

1187
00:43:56,901 --> 00:44:00,537
- I think I can backpack now.
- Right? You got this.

1188
00:44:00,538 --> 00:44:03,540
It's hard to bring
a suitcase to places like this.

1189
00:44:03,775 --> 00:44:06,377
I thought about it,
but I didn't think I could do it.

1190
00:44:06,378 --> 00:44:07,578
Because I have so much stuff.

1191
00:44:07,912 --> 00:44:09,279
But I think I can now.

1192
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:10,480
- Totally.
- Absolutely.

1193
00:44:10,748 --> 00:44:15,685
Taking pretty pictures used to be
my number one priority when traveling.

1194
00:44:15,686 --> 00:44:16,586
- Right.
- But,

1195
00:44:16,587 --> 00:44:17,919
that's not really the point.

1196
00:44:17,920 --> 00:44:21,758
Travel isn't about wearing
pretty clothes and taking pictures.

1197
00:44:21,759 --> 00:44:22,625
You're right.

1198
00:44:22,626 --> 00:44:25,028
- I think what I experience matters more.
- I agree.

1199
00:44:25,029 --> 00:44:28,632
That's why backpackers
just wear tank tops and pants...

1200
00:44:28,633 --> 00:44:30,501
Yes, just a pair of sweatpants.

1201
00:44:30,502 --> 00:44:32,802
No makeup, no fuss.

1202
00:44:32,803 --> 00:44:36,005
Maybe that actually makes
for a deeper travel experience.

1203
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:37,207
I agree.

1204
00:44:38,576 --> 00:44:41,611
- You can focus on the trip.
- Without worrying about all the stuff.

1205
00:44:41,612 --> 00:44:43,013
Exactly.

1206
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:45,182
You can focus on the moment.

1207
00:44:45,183 --> 00:44:49,720
- Then, I achieved my travel aesthetic.
- Backpacking aesthetic.

1208
00:44:50,088 --> 00:44:53,290
Like those European girls
with a backpack yesterday...

1209
00:44:53,291 --> 00:44:54,658
I should try it.

1210
00:44:54,659 --> 00:44:57,027
(With a lighter backpack,
the vibe is complete.)

1211
00:44:57,261 --> 00:44:58,563
(Thinking)

1212
00:44:58,564 --> 00:45:01,297
We're not actually supposed
to start a fire in the jungle, right?

1213
00:45:01,666 --> 00:45:02,865
Of course not.

1214
00:45:03,202 --> 00:45:04,901
There's a hotel.

1215
00:45:04,902 --> 00:45:06,736
We're staying at a resort.

1216
00:45:07,005 --> 00:45:09,542
- So, it'll be fine.
- Great.

1217
00:45:09,543 --> 00:45:10,508
(The place looked good online.)

1218
00:45:11,509 --> 00:45:13,310
I'm so excited to go to the jungle.

1219
00:45:13,311 --> 00:45:16,313
- Right?
- It's been on my bucket list.

1220
00:45:16,314 --> 00:45:18,482
- It suits you.
- Perfectly.

1221
00:45:18,850 --> 00:45:20,951
You look like Moana in the jungle.

1222
00:45:22,186 --> 00:45:25,688
(Filled with excitement,
the bus leaves the city.)

1223
00:45:26,657 --> 00:45:30,927
(The greenery gets thicker and thicker.)

1224
00:45:31,929 --> 00:45:35,031
(Bump)

1225
00:45:35,633 --> 00:45:39,636
(Bump)

1226
00:45:40,771 --> 00:45:47,177
(After waking up from the bumpy ride...)

1227
00:45:49,714 --> 00:45:50,815
(A dense palm forest stretches out.)

1228
00:45:50,816 --> 00:45:53,717
This is really the jungle.

1229
00:45:53,718 --> 00:45:56,286
It's jungle.

1230
00:45:56,287 --> 00:45:57,421
What if there are snakes?

1231
00:46:00,791 --> 00:46:03,059
This is a perfect jungle.

1232
00:46:03,595 --> 00:46:05,227
It feels like Tarzan could show up.

1233
00:46:05,630 --> 00:46:06,663
Come on, Tarzan.

1234
00:46:12,937 --> 00:46:16,439
<i>An unexpected blackout</i>

1235
00:46:17,041 --> 00:46:18,642
(From Tarzan to "Next Level")

1236
00:46:18,643 --> 00:46:20,277
I recognized it instantly.

1237
00:46:20,511 --> 00:46:21,978
(Happy)

1238
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:25,348
I've never seen this many palm trees.

1239
00:46:25,349 --> 00:46:26,816
- It's amazing.
- It's so organized.

1240
00:46:26,817 --> 00:46:28,094
(The endless forest road continues.)

1241
00:46:28,095 --> 00:46:29,185
All lined up in a row.

1242
00:46:30,188 --> 00:46:31,121
It's so cool.

1243
00:46:35,359 --> 00:46:36,693
It's completely different.

1244
00:46:37,428 --> 00:46:39,629
It looks nothing like
typical Southeast Asia.

1245
00:46:40,198 --> 00:46:42,032
Have you ever seen
scenery like this, Won Ji?

1246
00:46:42,033 --> 00:46:44,368
I've never seen a palm forest before.

1247
00:46:44,369 --> 00:46:46,003
- Right?
- Yes, it's a palm forest.

1248
00:46:46,004 --> 00:46:49,306
See? It's a sight even
a seasoned traveler rarely gets to see.

1249
00:46:50,374 --> 00:46:51,841
Come to think of it, that's true.

1250
00:46:51,842 --> 00:46:53,409
This is amazing.

1251
00:46:54,579 --> 00:46:56,379
There are cows.

1252
00:46:57,081 --> 00:46:58,114
They're so cute.

1253
00:46:58,516 --> 00:47:00,217
There are cows in the forest too.

1254
00:47:00,218 --> 00:47:01,351
There are so many.

1255
00:47:01,352 --> 00:47:03,954
- They're really free.
- What's this?

1256
00:47:04,122 --> 00:47:06,156
The combination of palm trees and cows.

1257
00:47:06,157 --> 00:47:08,992
(The cows relaxing in the sunlight)

1258
00:47:09,460 --> 00:47:13,273
The cows you see on our left...

1259
00:47:13,274 --> 00:47:14,665
(Suddenly playing tour guide)

1260
00:47:15,533 --> 00:47:18,668
They're free-range cows
enjoying their lives.

1261
00:47:18,903 --> 00:47:21,304
They relax in the sun
and live their best lives.

1262
00:47:21,839 --> 00:47:23,873
That's how they grow up here.

1263
00:47:24,743 --> 00:47:26,443
So they don't have owners?

1264
00:47:26,444 --> 00:47:27,444
No.

1265
00:47:28,212 --> 00:47:29,245
They all have owners.

1266
00:47:29,547 --> 00:47:30,447
Who owns them?

1267
00:47:33,651 --> 00:47:35,952
(This guide skips the questions
that she can't answer.)

1268
00:47:35,953 --> 00:47:38,121
They do have owners, but...

1269
00:47:38,146 --> 00:47:39,132
(After another two hours...)

1270
00:47:39,156 --> 00:47:40,824
Do they really have owners?

1271
00:47:43,628 --> 00:47:45,963
I guess people live together here.

1272
00:47:46,731 --> 00:47:49,165
Maybe people live close together here.

1273
00:47:49,167 --> 00:47:50,234
(The vehicle enters a village.)

1274
00:47:50,235 --> 00:47:51,835
- It's peaceful.
- Absolutely.

1275
00:47:52,036 --> 00:47:53,203
(Crossing a small bridge over the river)

1276
00:47:53,204 --> 00:47:54,337
It's such a happy village.

1277
00:47:55,006 --> 00:47:56,239
It must be so peaceful here.

1278
00:47:59,677 --> 00:48:00,543
Are we almost there?

1279
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:03,380
(Bukit Lawang signs begin appearing.)

1280
00:48:03,381 --> 00:48:04,281
What time is it?

1281
00:48:07,518 --> 00:48:08,718
I got a message.

1282
00:48:08,953 --> 00:48:12,656
"Take the accommodation's
pickup vehicle from here."

1283
00:48:13,190 --> 00:48:14,524
Pickup vehicle?

1284
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:17,592
- They have a pickup service too?
- I'm so excited.

1285
00:48:18,062 --> 00:48:20,964
- Nice resort.
- We're going to a resort.

1286
00:48:22,834 --> 00:48:25,401
Do we switch cars here?

1287
00:48:25,770 --> 00:48:26,737
I think so.

1288
00:48:27,505 --> 00:48:30,240
- We're arrived.
- Finally we're getting off.

1289
00:48:30,241 --> 00:48:32,008
(Bukit Lawang bus terminal)

1290
00:48:32,410 --> 00:48:35,180
(They finally arrive
in Bukit Lawang after three hours.)

1291
00:48:35,181 --> 00:48:37,147
Thank you so much.

1292
00:48:37,148 --> 00:48:40,450
(Total bus fare:
200,000 rupiah for four people)

1293
00:48:40,785 --> 00:48:44,154
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1294
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:45,622
- Is that it?
- Is that the one?

1295
00:48:45,623 --> 00:48:46,790
Yes, that's it.

1296
00:48:47,023 --> 00:48:48,658
That car is really nice.

1297
00:48:48,826 --> 00:48:52,061
- Of course. It's luxury.
- Resort vehicle.

1298
00:48:52,062 --> 00:48:54,197
Luxury has begun.

1299
00:48:54,899 --> 00:48:56,199
- Hello.
- Hello.

1300
00:48:56,901 --> 00:48:58,768
- Really?
- What's this?

1301
00:48:58,769 --> 00:49:02,006
(They board
the surprisingly fancy vehicle.)

1302
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:04,808
I'm so excited for the luxury resort.

1303
00:49:04,809 --> 00:49:07,544
Are we finally going to rest?

1304
00:49:07,545 --> 00:49:10,180
(They're getting way ahead of themselves.)

1305
00:49:10,315 --> 00:49:13,850
- I can't wait.
- I can't wait.

1306
00:49:13,851 --> 00:49:15,352
I'm so excited.

1307
00:49:18,789 --> 00:49:20,256
I can't wait.

1308
00:49:20,257 --> 00:49:22,034
I'm at my comfiest right now.

1309
00:49:22,035 --> 00:49:23,292
(A backpacker using
her backpack as a pillow)

1310
00:49:23,828 --> 00:49:25,929
(Deeper into the jungle)

1311
00:49:26,697 --> 00:49:27,898
We're here.

1312
00:49:27,923 --> 00:49:29,943
(They arrive
at their dream accommodation.)

1313
00:49:29,968 --> 00:49:31,569
Hurray.

1314
00:49:34,105 --> 00:49:36,440
- This is exciting.
- Hurray.

1315
00:49:38,709 --> 00:49:40,443
- I think that's it.
- It's good.

1316
00:49:42,446 --> 00:49:44,080
(A cool, quiet path through the forest)

1317
00:49:44,081 --> 00:49:45,648
It feels like we're in the woods.

1318
00:49:46,217 --> 00:49:47,117
Great.

1319
00:49:48,753 --> 00:49:49,586
I like it.

1320
00:49:49,820 --> 00:49:52,155
- The accommodation is so nice.
- I think it's here.

1321
00:49:52,823 --> 00:49:54,057
This is so nice.

1322
00:49:54,058 --> 00:49:56,559
I can already feel the air conditioning.

1323
00:49:56,962 --> 00:49:59,229
We'll shower, lie down.

1324
00:50:00,531 --> 00:50:01,831
(A small passageway comes into view.)

1325
00:50:01,899 --> 00:50:02,875
What is that?

1326
00:50:03,999 --> 00:50:05,542
Wait. Is this the wrong way?

1327
00:50:05,578 --> 00:50:07,146
The maximum...

1328
00:50:07,646 --> 00:50:08,914
is eight people.

1329
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:11,483
(Only eight people can go at a time.)

1330
00:50:11,517 --> 00:50:13,352
- What is that?
- What does that mean?

1331
00:50:13,953 --> 00:50:16,088
There must be a limit
on how many people can be on the bridge.

1332
00:50:16,089 --> 00:50:17,623
- That bridge?
- Yes.

1333
00:50:18,944 --> 00:50:22,157
(They have to cross the wooden bridge.)

1334
00:50:22,257 --> 00:50:23,762
Why is the bridge swaying so much?

1335
00:50:23,996 --> 00:50:26,165
I get so anxious about those things.

1336
00:50:26,311 --> 00:50:28,100
We always have to cross a bridge.

1337
00:50:28,101 --> 00:50:31,224
(It shakes
even with the slightest movement.)

1338
00:50:31,334 --> 00:50:33,573
You can't get to your lodging
without crossing a bridge on this show.

1339
00:50:34,859 --> 00:50:35,908
Wherever we go.

1340
00:50:36,928 --> 00:50:39,274
(It just happened to be that way.)

1341
00:50:39,313 --> 00:50:42,581
- Let's go.
- What if it's shakier than we think?

1342
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:43,816
It looks fine.

1343
00:50:43,853 --> 00:50:44,950
Do you think so?

1344
00:50:44,951 --> 00:50:48,347
(Stepping onto the wooden bridge)

1345
00:50:48,754 --> 00:50:50,754
- Now...
- It looks sturdy.

1346
00:50:50,755 --> 00:50:52,255
It's fine so far.

1347
00:50:52,256 --> 00:50:53,892
It's fine for now?

1348
00:50:54,088 --> 00:50:55,427
It's not sturdy.

1349
00:50:55,428 --> 00:50:57,162
(The bridge is shaky
as soon as they say it's fine.)

1350
00:50:57,522 --> 00:50:59,098
It doesn't look sturdy.

1351
00:50:59,568 --> 00:51:00,566
Let's go slowly.

1352
00:51:00,567 --> 00:51:03,202
This is a wooden bridge.

1353
00:51:04,307 --> 00:51:06,505
The bridge to the elephant hotel
was a metal bridge.

1354
00:51:06,506 --> 00:51:08,340
It's swaying.

1355
00:51:09,367 --> 00:51:11,610
There are gaps here and there.

1356
00:51:12,378 --> 00:51:14,279
So be careful.

1357
00:51:14,313 --> 00:51:16,115
You can see everything underneath.

1358
00:51:16,433 --> 00:51:17,282
Like this.

1359
00:51:17,313 --> 00:51:19,051
(Exclaiming)

1360
00:51:19,385 --> 00:51:20,753
My goodness.

1361
00:51:20,779 --> 00:51:22,287
(Still long way to go)

1362
00:51:24,023 --> 00:51:25,391
If you fall...

1363
00:51:26,284 --> 00:51:28,761
But the river is not that deep.

1364
00:51:28,777 --> 00:51:31,930
It's lower than the one
to the elephant hotel.

1365
00:51:31,976 --> 00:51:32,684
It's lower.

1366
00:51:32,685 --> 00:51:34,366
So it's not that scary.

1367
00:51:36,597 --> 00:51:37,903
It's not that shaky.

1368
00:51:37,904 --> 00:51:40,039
- It's not that bad.
- The water is so clear.

1369
00:51:41,351 --> 00:51:42,574
It's nice.

1370
00:51:44,343 --> 00:51:46,345
I want to jump in!

1371
00:51:46,346 --> 00:51:47,537
(Cool wind blows.)

1372
00:51:51,116 --> 00:51:53,030
It reminds me of chicken soup.

1373
00:51:53,031 --> 00:51:55,546
- I want to eat chicken soup.
- I totally get it.

1374
00:51:56,155 --> 00:52:00,192
It's like we're visiting Eoreumgol
in Miryang.

1375
00:52:02,474 --> 00:52:03,605
It's not scary.

1376
00:52:03,606 --> 00:52:04,678
Maybe a little scary.

1377
00:52:04,741 --> 00:52:06,298
Be careful.

1378
00:52:07,188 --> 00:52:08,500
- Wait.
- Watch out.

1379
00:52:09,201 --> 00:52:10,708
I'm glad we don't have our suitcase today.

1380
00:52:10,709 --> 00:52:11,837
I know.

1381
00:52:11,838 --> 00:52:13,172
I can imagine dragging a suitcase here.

1382
00:52:13,512 --> 00:52:14,332
We made it.

1383
00:52:14,368 --> 00:52:15,407
Hello.

1384
00:52:16,075 --> 00:52:18,277
- Hello.
- Hello.

1385
00:52:19,084 --> 00:52:22,891
(They literally crossed mountains
and rivers to make it here.)

1386
00:52:22,970 --> 00:52:26,257
- Check in, please.
- You can check in over there.

1387
00:52:26,284 --> 00:52:27,397
Check in.

1388
00:52:27,422 --> 00:52:28,311
- Okay.
- Follow me.

1389
00:52:30,312 --> 00:52:31,924
This place is so nice.

1390
00:52:32,867 --> 00:52:33,968
It looks like paradise.

1391
00:52:33,993 --> 00:52:35,194
- Paradise.
- It's so nice.

1392
00:52:35,273 --> 00:52:36,328
It's cool.

1393
00:52:36,807 --> 00:52:39,064
- What is this place?
- Goodness.

1394
00:52:39,100 --> 00:52:40,833
Thank you.

1395
00:52:41,113 --> 00:52:43,535
- I want to stay here for more days.
- It's really nice.

1396
00:52:44,153 --> 00:52:47,538
- It's nice. That must be the front desk.
- It's so pretty.

1397
00:52:47,539 --> 00:52:49,108
I love the interior here.

1398
00:52:50,653 --> 00:52:51,810
Antique.

1399
00:52:51,811 --> 00:52:55,587
(The bamboo front desk
brings out the Indonesian vibe.)

1400
00:52:56,315 --> 00:52:57,516
Fantastic.

1401
00:52:57,983 --> 00:53:01,220
- Fantastic.
- This place is beautiful.

1402
00:53:01,474 --> 00:53:02,788
You can go check in over there.

1403
00:53:02,789 --> 00:53:04,436
- This is my style.
- Thank you.

1404
00:53:04,437 --> 00:53:05,891
- My style!
- Thank you so much.

1405
00:53:05,892 --> 00:53:07,392
It's beautiful!

1406
00:53:07,616 --> 00:53:09,695
- There's a souvenir shop.
- A souvenir shop.

1407
00:53:10,462 --> 00:53:12,998
That wooden orangutan mask is so cute!

1408
00:53:14,032 --> 00:53:16,032
They're orangutans!

1409
00:53:16,033 --> 00:53:18,761
(A symbol of Bukit Lawang,
Orangutan magnets)

1410
00:53:18,994 --> 00:53:19,805
Awesome.

1411
00:53:20,873 --> 00:53:22,141
I want to buy one.

1412
00:53:22,775 --> 00:53:24,543
This is the front desk.

1413
00:53:27,212 --> 00:53:28,514
We'd like to check in.

1414
00:53:28,773 --> 00:53:30,082
Do you need our passports?

1415
00:53:30,386 --> 00:53:33,218
Yes, but the room is not ready yet.

1416
00:53:34,052 --> 00:53:36,877
You can check in around 1 or 2 p.m.

1417
00:53:37,049 --> 00:53:39,116
Okay. Around 1 or 2 p.m.

1418
00:53:39,424 --> 00:53:41,393
We still have some time, then.

1419
00:53:41,463 --> 00:53:44,630
Until then, you can have breakfast.

1420
00:53:44,631 --> 00:53:45,397
Okay.

1421
00:53:45,398 --> 00:53:47,166
That sounds great.

1422
00:53:47,167 --> 00:53:48,834
- We can eat first.
- Sounds perfect.

1423
00:53:48,835 --> 00:53:51,036
Thank you.

1424
00:53:52,022 --> 00:53:53,572
Let's eat while we wait.

1425
00:53:54,215 --> 00:53:56,041
- I like that.
- It's amazing.

1426
00:53:56,042 --> 00:53:57,976
- This place is my favorite so far.
- Mine too.

1427
00:53:58,215 --> 00:54:02,012
It's not too hot or sunny.

1428
00:54:02,013 --> 00:54:04,216
- It's so lush and green.
- It's so nice.

1429
00:54:04,217 --> 00:54:05,017
Mother Nature!

1430
00:54:05,018 --> 00:54:06,285
Where should we sit?

1431
00:54:06,764 --> 00:54:08,554
- How about here?
- Shall we sit on the terrace?

1432
00:54:08,555 --> 00:54:10,881
(Sitting on the terrace)

1433
00:54:11,181 --> 00:54:14,226
I said I'd pay extra
and asked for one of each.

1434
00:54:14,961 --> 00:54:17,108
(That sounds great!)

1435
00:54:17,221 --> 00:54:19,331
- Things are cheap here.
- That sounds good.

1436
00:54:19,332 --> 00:54:20,734
(It's time to eat.)

1437
00:54:20,914 --> 00:54:21,900
Okay.

1438
00:54:23,847 --> 00:54:24,867
(Glancing)

1439
00:54:24,927 --> 00:54:28,640
I'm filming a sparrow
because it looks so cute.

1440
00:54:28,641 --> 00:54:31,038
(Cute!)

1441
00:54:31,798 --> 00:54:33,645
I can hear the water.

1442
00:54:33,670 --> 00:54:35,354
This is insane. I love it here.

1443
00:54:36,081 --> 00:54:39,451
It feels like we're at a stream.

1444
00:54:41,563 --> 00:54:42,888
I do want to swim.

1445
00:54:42,889 --> 00:54:44,289
I really want to jump into the water.

1446
00:54:44,290 --> 00:54:46,091
I want to jump in too. It looks so clean.

1447
00:54:46,092 --> 00:54:47,125
I know!

1448
00:54:47,126 --> 00:54:49,239
(A refreshing river is flowing
right in front of us.)

1449
00:54:49,240 --> 00:54:53,699
It's summer,
and we're already on day 6 or 7,

1450
00:54:53,780 --> 00:54:55,580
- but we haven't gone swimming yet!
- We've never gone swimming.

1451
00:54:55,581 --> 00:54:57,102
We haven't gone swimming.

1452
00:54:57,187 --> 00:54:59,204
Is it day 7 or 8?

1453
00:54:59,819 --> 00:55:01,673
I think so. Let me check.

1454
00:55:01,707 --> 00:55:02,708
It's day seven.

1455
00:55:02,747 --> 00:55:04,794
- We don't look at the time.
- We know nothing.

1456
00:55:04,841 --> 00:55:07,546
I've disconnected from the outside world.

1457
00:55:09,201 --> 00:55:10,415
That's so funny.

1458
00:55:10,467 --> 00:55:12,818
- I've disconnected from the world.
- "I've disconnected."

1459
00:55:13,185 --> 00:55:14,720
It's day seven.

1460
00:55:15,087 --> 00:55:16,889
- Seven?
- Only day seven?

1461
00:55:16,890 --> 00:55:18,657
I feel like it's been seven months.

1462
00:55:18,787 --> 00:55:19,913
Seven months?

1463
00:55:20,173 --> 00:55:22,561
We've made it pretty far, then.

1464
00:55:22,653 --> 00:55:26,027
- It's already been a week.
- We're halfway through.

1465
00:55:26,087 --> 00:55:28,087
We've been together for a week.

1466
00:55:28,088 --> 00:55:29,568
We haven't been apart for a single moment!

1467
00:55:30,288 --> 00:55:32,529
(That's true!)

1468
00:55:36,908 --> 00:55:40,800
(Celebrating with an elephanT-trunk pose)

1469
00:55:40,873 --> 00:55:42,614
By the way,
I haven't spent a whole week...

1470
00:55:43,582 --> 00:55:46,018
with someone in a long time.

1471
00:55:46,053 --> 00:55:47,319
With someone.

1472
00:55:47,320 --> 00:55:48,053
Right.

1473
00:55:48,073 --> 00:55:49,321
- With someone.
- With someone.

1474
00:55:49,368 --> 00:55:51,256
- And we were total strangers.
- Exactly.

1475
00:55:51,857 --> 00:55:54,259
I haven't had this experience in a while.

1476
00:55:54,509 --> 00:55:55,975
I know.

1477
00:55:57,075 --> 00:56:01,841
(Halfway through the trip, they realize
how special their time together has been.)

1478
00:56:04,908 --> 00:56:06,381
That's huge!

1479
00:56:06,441 --> 00:56:08,707
- Thank you.
- That looks so good.

1480
00:56:08,974 --> 00:56:10,509
(Our lifeline!)

1481
00:56:11,254 --> 00:56:13,528
(Their tone becomes softer.)

1482
00:56:13,529 --> 00:56:15,113
Thank you very much!

1483
00:56:15,114 --> 00:56:19,001
(A cup of iced coffee
in a place with fresh air)

1484
00:56:19,481 --> 00:56:20,652
Thank you.

1485
00:56:20,653 --> 00:56:22,721
(Gulping)

1486
00:56:23,555 --> 00:56:24,756
That hits the spot.

1487
00:56:26,140 --> 00:56:27,326
Oh, dear!

1488
00:56:27,592 --> 00:56:29,592
- It's refreshing.
- It's nutty.

1489
00:56:32,360 --> 00:56:33,332
It's good.

1490
00:56:34,607 --> 00:56:36,433
It's so good!

1491
00:56:36,740 --> 00:56:37,836
It's really good.

1492
00:56:38,060 --> 00:56:40,172
You're really good!

1493
00:56:40,173 --> 00:56:41,301
(The youngest follows the older.)

1494
00:56:41,887 --> 00:56:43,964
You're so good!

1495
00:56:43,965 --> 00:56:44,795
(And the oldest follows the youngest.)

1496
00:56:45,313 --> 00:56:46,645
How am I doing?

1497
00:56:46,706 --> 00:56:48,313
- You're doing a good job.
- I am?

1498
00:56:48,540 --> 00:56:49,982
You've come a long way with us.

1499
00:56:49,983 --> 00:56:52,584
You're almost at our energy level!

1500
00:56:54,400 --> 00:56:55,988
"Almost at our energy level!"

1501
00:56:56,040 --> 00:56:57,422
Almost at our energy level!

1502
00:56:57,423 --> 00:56:58,557
- That was...
- That was good, right?

1503
00:56:58,686 --> 00:57:01,860
- You even sounded like them.
- I got a lot better, right?

1504
00:57:02,227 --> 00:57:04,486
- I've been paying attention to Harimu.
- I see.

1505
00:57:04,487 --> 00:57:06,063
(It takes only 7 days for Won Ji
to be Harimu.)

1506
00:57:06,064 --> 00:57:07,165
Almost!

1507
00:57:07,566 --> 00:57:08,767
Something is coming.

1508
00:57:08,792 --> 00:57:14,262
(Their first breakfast in Indonesia)

1509
00:57:14,639 --> 00:57:16,141
That looks good.

1510
00:57:16,142 --> 00:57:18,810
What is this? It's awesome.

1511
00:57:19,599 --> 00:57:21,826
What is this? It's a bamboo leaf.

1512
00:57:21,827 --> 00:57:23,982
- That looks good.
- It looks pretty.

1513
00:57:24,520 --> 00:57:27,085
- Let's dig in!
- Let's dig in!

1514
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:33,594
(Taking a bite of nasi goreng
with an egg on top)

1515
00:57:34,014 --> 00:57:35,193
It's delicious.

1516
00:57:35,194 --> 00:57:36,361
I'm fully enjoying this morning.

1517
00:57:37,047 --> 00:57:38,725
(One bite of sweet and savory mie goreng)

1518
00:57:38,726 --> 00:57:41,600
Their fried rice tastes different
from Thai fried rice.

1519
00:57:41,867 --> 00:57:43,268
It's indeed different.

1520
00:57:44,073 --> 00:57:45,203
It's delicious.

1521
00:57:46,705 --> 00:57:48,907
We can take our time with breakfast.

1522
00:57:51,032 --> 00:57:52,298
This one is good.

1523
00:57:52,944 --> 00:57:56,724
We haven't had breakfast like this before,
have we?

1524
00:57:56,725 --> 00:57:58,917
We've never had breakfast
this beautiful before.

1525
00:57:59,271 --> 00:58:00,385
You're right.

1526
00:58:00,386 --> 00:58:04,305
(Maybe good breakfasts are
the best part of traveling.)

1527
00:58:05,123 --> 00:58:06,625
The pineapple is so good.

1528
00:58:06,892 --> 00:58:08,693
Are pineapples just really good
in Indonesia?

1529
00:58:09,667 --> 00:58:11,129
It's so yummy. I'm happy.

1530
00:58:13,165 --> 00:58:14,803
They also say...

1531
00:58:14,804 --> 00:58:16,868
this kind of phrase a lot.

1532
00:58:16,869 --> 00:58:19,171
(Someone is approaching.)

1533
00:58:19,464 --> 00:58:20,472
I got it.

1534
00:58:20,473 --> 00:58:21,540
Excuse me.

1535
00:58:22,140 --> 00:58:23,141
Excuse me.

1536
00:58:23,604 --> 00:58:25,043
Hi.

1537
00:58:27,679 --> 00:58:28,847
Hello. I'm your guide.

1538
00:58:30,544 --> 00:58:31,817
My name is Ipu.

1539
00:58:31,837 --> 00:58:33,218
- I'm pretty?
- Our guide?

1540
00:58:33,219 --> 00:58:34,352
Hello.

1541
00:58:34,353 --> 00:58:35,921
Nice to meet you.

1542
00:58:35,960 --> 00:58:38,123
- Nice to meet you.
- What guide?

1543
00:58:39,240 --> 00:58:41,440
I'll tell you a little about the jungle.

1544
00:58:41,987 --> 00:58:43,560
(Right now?)

1545
00:58:44,129 --> 00:58:46,813
When you go to the jungle,

1546
00:58:46,926 --> 00:58:48,967
you'll see orangutans...

1547
00:58:49,313 --> 00:58:51,736
- and monkeys.
- Orangutans!

1548
00:58:52,082 --> 00:58:56,589
I can also show you plants
like coffee trees.

1549
00:58:57,262 --> 00:58:59,796
So we can see a lot of animals, right?

1550
00:59:00,102 --> 00:59:01,279
That's right.

1551
00:59:01,316 --> 00:59:02,681
Right?

1552
00:59:02,856 --> 00:59:04,049
The jungle...

1553
00:59:04,956 --> 00:59:07,886
Are we going to the jungle today?

1554
00:59:08,420 --> 00:59:09,488
Today.

1555
00:59:10,442 --> 00:59:12,528
(They're going today.)

1556
00:59:12,662 --> 00:59:13,784
Was it today?

1557
00:59:13,785 --> 00:59:14,995
(I thought we could take some rest.)

1558
00:59:15,374 --> 00:59:16,753
You're going to the jungle today...

1559
00:59:16,754 --> 00:59:18,488
- Today?
- and sleep there too.

1560
00:59:18,708 --> 00:59:20,165
- Sleep in the jungle?
- Yes!

1561
00:59:20,166 --> 00:59:21,333
Not here?

1562
00:59:21,334 --> 00:59:22,667
What is he talking about?

1563
00:59:23,053 --> 00:59:24,269
But this is the jungle.

1564
00:59:24,326 --> 00:59:26,339
No. This is a restaurant.

1565
00:59:26,933 --> 00:59:29,879
(Ipu starts telling them the truth.)

1566
00:59:29,946 --> 00:59:32,666
But the crew said we'd check in here.

1567
00:59:33,078 --> 00:59:35,780
We check in at 1 p.m.

1568
00:59:36,641 --> 00:59:38,048
I don't think so.

1569
00:59:38,754 --> 00:59:40,721
You said "No." Really?

1570
00:59:40,801 --> 00:59:42,988
- So we don't sleep here?
- No.

1571
00:59:44,721 --> 00:59:46,122
Why?

1572
00:59:46,123 --> 00:59:47,359
Why?

1573
00:59:47,823 --> 00:59:48,994
The jungle is the best.

1574
00:59:49,016 --> 00:59:50,829
- Oh, dear.
- He says the jungle is the best.

1575
00:59:52,256 --> 00:59:54,023
Do you have any hotels in the jungle?

1576
00:59:54,024 --> 00:59:55,400
No.

1577
00:59:55,401 --> 00:59:56,701
Only camps.

1578
00:59:57,721 --> 00:59:59,408
Do we sleep in a tent, then?

1579
00:59:59,454 --> 01:00:00,639
Yes. In a tent.

1580
01:00:01,398 --> 01:00:02,098
(Frozen)

1581
01:00:02,099 --> 01:00:05,034
You might even spot
giant lizards out there.

1582
01:00:05,436 --> 01:00:07,870
There are monkeys and bugs too.

1583
01:00:08,538 --> 01:00:09,539
(Today's roommates:
giant lizards, monkeys, and bugs)

1584
01:00:09,540 --> 01:00:12,040
Can we shower there?

1585
01:00:12,041 --> 01:00:15,143
Sure. You can wash off in the river
while you swim.

1586
01:00:15,144 --> 01:00:17,546
(Nature's own shower)

1587
01:00:17,547 --> 01:00:19,548
- Shower in the...
- In the jungle, yeah.

1588
01:00:20,384 --> 01:00:23,351
(Even Moana didn't see this coming.)

1589
01:00:23,352 --> 01:00:25,087
We didn't expect this.

1590
01:00:25,557 --> 01:00:26,490
You feel good?

1591
01:00:26,857 --> 01:00:27,722
Wow.

1592
01:00:28,091 --> 01:00:29,491
- Yeah.
- Yep.

1593
01:00:30,027 --> 01:00:31,227
(Hard pass)

1594
01:00:31,228 --> 01:00:32,595
Then again,

1595
01:00:32,938 --> 01:00:35,398
- you never know until you try.
- Okay.

1596
01:00:36,867 --> 01:00:39,501
- Wait, she's leaving!
- Hold on!

1597
01:00:39,836 --> 01:00:42,338
I think I'll tap out here. Sorry, guys.

1598
01:00:42,339 --> 01:00:45,007
This feels like the perfect time
to turn back.

1599
01:00:45,542 --> 01:00:47,843
"Sleep in the jungle," he says.

1600
01:00:47,844 --> 01:00:49,845
Wait, can I...

1601
01:00:50,313 --> 01:00:51,613
use my phone out there?

1602
01:00:52,425 --> 01:00:53,525
- In the jungle...
- Is there reception?

1603
01:00:53,550 --> 01:00:57,453
There's no signal, no Wi-Fi, no lights.

1604
01:00:57,478 --> 01:01:00,136
(No internet, no Wi-Fi, no lights)

1605
01:01:00,524 --> 01:01:02,224
- No electricity at all?
- None.

1606
01:01:02,225 --> 01:01:03,525
What?

1607
01:01:03,593 --> 01:01:06,629
The bathroom situation is another story.
It's pretty rough.

1608
01:01:06,630 --> 01:01:08,196
Wait, there's no real toilet?

1609
01:01:08,499 --> 01:01:09,332
No toilet?

1610
01:01:09,333 --> 01:01:11,734
- Nothing proper.
- Apparently it's pretty grim.

1611
01:01:11,735 --> 01:01:13,169
Is there at least "something"?

1612
01:01:13,703 --> 01:01:15,504
I doubt it.

1613
01:01:16,239 --> 01:01:18,208
I have a feeling nature is our toilet.

1614
01:01:18,842 --> 01:01:20,275
Check out this scar.

1615
01:01:20,510 --> 01:01:21,378
Was it a monkey?

1616
01:01:21,403 --> 01:01:23,009
(Showing off his scar all of a sudden)

1617
01:01:23,046 --> 01:01:24,313
- An orangutan?
- No.

1618
01:01:24,748 --> 01:01:25,681
A tiger?

1619
01:01:25,682 --> 01:01:26,515
Not a tiger.

1620
01:01:27,317 --> 01:01:29,218
- A snake?
- Yes.

1621
01:01:29,219 --> 01:01:30,119
A king cobra.

1622
01:01:32,022 --> 01:01:33,389
- A king cobra?
- A king cobra?

1623
01:01:34,391 --> 01:01:36,859
(Wait, what did he say?)

1624
01:01:36,860 --> 01:01:38,328
It happened 20 years ago.

1625
01:01:39,296 --> 01:01:42,331
A king cobra bit his arm.

1626
01:01:42,499 --> 01:01:45,401
He still doesn't have full use of it.

1627
01:01:45,402 --> 01:01:46,368
He's okay, right?

1628
01:01:47,104 --> 01:01:49,406
I can't die out here, you know.

1629
01:01:49,407 --> 01:01:51,174
I still have so much to live for!

1630
01:01:52,109 --> 01:01:53,476
Are we really going to be okay?

1631
01:01:57,180 --> 01:02:00,082
He got bit by a king cobra
and almost died.

1632
01:02:00,484 --> 01:02:01,350
I'm still kicking, though.

1633
01:02:01,651 --> 01:02:05,487
So there really are
wild king cobras out here.

1634
01:02:05,755 --> 01:02:07,522
And he's just shrugging it off.

1635
01:02:08,425 --> 01:02:09,925
Can you ask him how far the camp is?

1636
01:02:09,926 --> 01:02:14,363
How long until we get
to where we're staying?

1637
01:02:14,364 --> 01:02:16,732
Probably around five hours.

1638
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:17,666
Five hours?

1639
01:02:18,401 --> 01:02:20,202
Five hours trekking through the jungle?

1640
01:02:21,071 --> 01:02:22,138
Lots of uphills and downhills.

1641
01:02:22,139 --> 01:02:23,839
- For five straight hours?
- Wow.

1642
01:02:24,008 --> 01:02:25,341
Do you live out here?

1643
01:02:25,342 --> 01:02:28,544
No, I used to live in the jungle.

1644
01:02:28,569 --> 01:02:29,869
I live in a village now.

1645
01:02:30,214 --> 01:02:32,848
Sometimes when I head into the jungle,

1646
01:02:32,849 --> 01:02:33,816
I'll stay for ten days.

1647
01:02:33,817 --> 01:02:35,117
Ten days?

1648
01:02:35,352 --> 01:02:36,552
(Awed)

1649
01:02:36,553 --> 01:02:37,887
Sometimes even a month.

1650
01:02:39,055 --> 01:02:39,954
(A whole month in the jungle)

1651
01:02:39,955 --> 01:02:42,357
He'll go in for ten days,
sometimes up to a full month.

1652
01:02:42,625 --> 01:02:45,694
All right, I'll meet you
out front shortly.

1653
01:02:45,695 --> 01:02:46,996
- Sounds good.
- Okay, thank you.

1654
01:02:46,997 --> 01:02:48,063
See you soon!

1655
01:02:48,064 --> 01:02:48,831
See you.

1656
01:02:48,856 --> 01:02:50,890
- Bye!
- See you soon!

1657
01:02:51,168 --> 01:02:52,568
(Hitting high notes)

1658
01:02:53,370 --> 01:02:56,205
Let's eat up and hit the road.

1659
01:02:56,206 --> 01:02:56,906
- Okay.
- Yeah.

1660
01:02:56,931 --> 01:02:58,808
(Last meal before entering the wild)

1661
01:02:59,209 --> 01:03:00,977
That took a second to process.

1662
01:03:02,479 --> 01:03:03,712
Let's get moving.

1663
01:03:04,247 --> 01:03:05,581
Before we head out,

1664
01:03:05,844 --> 01:03:07,365
we need to sort through our gear.

1665
01:03:07,390 --> 01:03:09,618
I mean, he said there's no power at all.

1666
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:11,987
- Right, we have to unpack this.
- And we can't even shower.

1667
01:03:11,988 --> 01:03:13,322
We bought shampoo yesterday.

1668
01:03:13,323 --> 01:03:15,457
- Why'd we even buy it?
- Leave it behind.

1669
01:03:15,458 --> 01:03:16,659
Are we brushing our teeth?

1670
01:03:16,660 --> 01:03:18,060
We definitely have to do that.

1671
01:03:18,061 --> 01:03:19,361
Toss them in here.

1672
01:03:19,362 --> 01:03:20,896
- Toothpaste.
- Got it.

1673
01:03:21,798 --> 01:03:23,031
Do we need lotion?

1674
01:03:23,032 --> 01:03:24,699
Let's just bring one bottle.

1675
01:03:24,700 --> 01:03:25,968
- What about sunscreen?
- In the bag.

1676
01:03:25,969 --> 01:03:26,835
Okay.

1677
01:03:26,836 --> 01:03:27,970
What about a jacket?

1678
01:03:28,538 --> 01:03:30,039
In case it gets chilly?

1679
01:03:30,040 --> 01:03:31,273
Let's just tie it around our waists.

1680
01:03:31,274 --> 01:03:32,274
Good idea, tie it on.

1681
01:03:32,275 --> 01:03:33,612
We have four towels.

1682
01:03:33,613 --> 01:03:34,510
Spare clothes.

1683
01:03:35,378 --> 01:03:38,280
- I think we'll need swimsuits.
- Packed. Underwear too.

1684
01:03:38,348 --> 01:03:40,082
Should we bring a handkerchief?

1685
01:03:40,717 --> 01:03:43,352
- Can I borrow it?
- Yes, go ahead.

1686
01:03:43,887 --> 01:03:45,964
(Sharing became familiar now.)

1687
01:03:45,989 --> 01:03:47,990
- Look at this.
- Our bags are actually getting lighter.

1688
01:03:48,325 --> 01:03:49,224
Right?

1689
01:03:49,659 --> 01:03:51,293
Should we ditch the swimsuits too?

1690
01:03:51,395 --> 01:03:53,863
- Should we?
- Why would we even need them?

1691
01:03:53,864 --> 01:03:55,464
We're not on a resort vacation!

1692
01:03:55,465 --> 01:03:57,500
It's not like there's an indoor pool.

1693
01:03:57,501 --> 01:03:58,701
- Valid point.
- Yeah.

1694
01:03:58,702 --> 01:03:59,869
What were we thinking?

1695
01:04:00,137 --> 01:04:02,471
Snap out of it. Swimsuit, my foot!

1696
01:04:02,472 --> 01:04:04,006
A swimsuit? What a luxury.

1697
01:04:04,007 --> 01:04:05,341
Where did we put it?

1698
01:04:06,310 --> 01:04:07,310
I'll pull them out.

1699
01:04:07,311 --> 01:04:08,412
- Take them out!
- On it.

1700
01:04:08,413 --> 01:04:10,046
- Are we just going to wear these?
- Yeah.

1701
01:04:10,071 --> 01:04:11,071
- Long pants?
- Yes.

1702
01:04:11,547 --> 01:04:12,848
We took out so much stuff.

1703
01:04:12,916 --> 01:04:13,949
We don't need any of it!

1704
01:04:14,451 --> 01:04:15,384
What about this flashlight?

1705
01:04:15,653 --> 01:04:16,951
- That's a must.
- We definitely need this.

1706
01:04:16,952 --> 01:04:19,421
We'll need it for bathroom runs
in the dark.

1707
01:04:19,422 --> 01:04:21,523
What a must-have.

1708
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:23,292
This is hilarious.

1709
01:04:23,293 --> 01:04:25,227
- Whose is this?
- Who tried to unpack this again?

1710
01:04:25,228 --> 01:04:26,695
We've been trying to ditch it
since day one.

1711
01:04:26,696 --> 01:04:27,964
- Yet it survives.
- Who tried to ditch it?

1712
01:04:27,965 --> 01:04:30,432
Hey, I've loved this thing from the start!

1713
01:04:31,034 --> 01:04:32,568
Now try lifting the bag.

1714
01:04:32,569 --> 01:04:34,003
- It's so light!
- Really?

1715
01:04:34,004 --> 01:04:34,837
What a relief.

1716
01:04:34,872 --> 01:04:37,373
Wow, this feels like
an ordinary school backpack now.

1717
01:04:37,907 --> 01:04:39,107
Off to school, Mom!

1718
01:04:39,108 --> 01:04:40,275
See you after class!

1719
01:04:40,644 --> 01:04:43,084
Four grown women,
and this is all our luggage?

1720
01:04:43,109 --> 01:04:43,912
This is wild.

1721
01:04:44,214 --> 01:04:46,114
By the way, I heard earlier...

1722
01:04:46,115 --> 01:04:48,450
they have porters here.

1723
01:04:48,719 --> 01:04:49,852
- Amazing!
- Really?

1724
01:04:49,853 --> 01:04:51,854
I used porters when I went trekking
in the Himalayas.

1725
01:04:51,855 --> 01:04:53,555
I mean, we're total beginners.

1726
01:04:53,556 --> 01:04:55,991
- It'd be way too brutal otherwise.
- We need to conserve our energy.

1727
01:04:55,992 --> 01:04:58,026
Our porter is going to love us.

1728
01:04:58,027 --> 01:04:59,328
The bag is feather-light.

1729
01:04:59,564 --> 01:05:01,330
Seriously light.

1730
01:05:01,331 --> 01:05:05,167
- Thank you!
- Thank you so much!

1731
01:05:06,036 --> 01:05:07,870
Let's do this.

1732
01:05:07,871 --> 01:05:11,641
- All right, let's move!
- To the jungle!

1733
01:05:11,642 --> 01:05:13,843
(Off to the jungle!)

1734
01:05:14,244 --> 01:05:15,044
(Ipu was waiting.)

1735
01:05:15,045 --> 01:05:16,613
- I'm ready.
- I'm Ipu.

1736
01:05:16,980 --> 01:05:17,980
Ipu!

1737
01:05:17,981 --> 01:05:19,581
Nice to meet you!

1738
01:05:19,582 --> 01:05:21,017
Oh, that's his name!

1739
01:05:21,018 --> 01:05:23,218
I thought he was calling me pretty.

1740
01:05:23,753 --> 01:05:26,422
You can call me One. Number one!

1741
01:05:26,423 --> 01:05:28,391
Number two!

1742
01:05:28,392 --> 01:05:29,358
Four!

1743
01:05:29,994 --> 01:05:31,093
I'm number five!

1744
01:05:31,094 --> 01:05:32,528
(I'll claim five, then.)

1745
01:05:32,762 --> 01:05:34,263
Number zero!

1746
01:05:34,631 --> 01:05:36,198
- His name is Ipu.
- Ipu.

1747
01:05:36,199 --> 01:05:37,233
That's such a cool name.

1748
01:05:37,400 --> 01:05:39,137
- Ipu!
- Ipu!

1749
01:05:39,138 --> 01:05:40,736
Wait, I just realized...

1750
01:05:40,804 --> 01:05:42,538
the crew is right behind us.

1751
01:05:42,772 --> 01:05:44,206
- That's reassuring.
- Let's go!

1752
01:05:45,442 --> 01:05:47,109
The stairs start right over there.

1753
01:05:47,110 --> 01:05:48,411
Look at those steps.

1754
01:05:48,980 --> 01:05:51,112
- Guys.
- Yes?

1755
01:05:51,113 --> 01:05:53,382
Check out our guide's shoes.

1756
01:05:54,150 --> 01:05:55,383
He's in flip-flops.

1757
01:05:55,384 --> 01:05:56,318
Now that's an absolute pro.

1758
01:05:56,319 --> 01:05:57,452
(Hiking in flip-flops)

1759
01:05:57,754 --> 01:05:59,621
Literally goals.

1760
01:05:59,622 --> 01:06:01,190
Here we go.

1761
01:06:01,191 --> 01:06:03,125
(The trail begins.)

1762
01:06:03,259 --> 01:06:06,127
Wait, shouldn't we take a photo
before we step in?

1763
01:06:06,128 --> 01:06:08,230
- I'll take it.
- Perfect.

1764
01:06:08,398 --> 01:06:09,965
Like a before-and-after shot.

1765
01:06:09,966 --> 01:06:10,699
Okay.

1766
01:06:11,534 --> 01:06:14,435
(One last photo in civilization)

1767
01:06:14,436 --> 01:06:16,005
- Got it.
- Let's grab a quick video too.

1768
01:06:16,239 --> 01:06:17,240
(Meanwhile...)

1769
01:06:17,241 --> 01:06:18,073
You're nailing it.

1770
01:06:18,311 --> 01:06:19,808
We're basically ready for bed.

1771
01:06:20,777 --> 01:06:22,811
What do they call this again?
Proof of life?

1772
01:06:23,146 --> 01:06:24,680
- Proof of life!
- Proof of life!

1773
01:06:24,681 --> 01:06:25,948
We're still alive and well.

1774
01:06:25,949 --> 01:06:29,184
(Setting his pack down suddenly)

1775
01:06:30,820 --> 01:06:34,122
(Taking off his glasses)

1776
01:06:34,491 --> 01:06:36,358
Time to switch modes.

1777
01:06:39,028 --> 01:06:42,330
(Taking off his shirt)

1778
01:06:42,632 --> 01:06:44,567
(The city girls vibe on,
blissfully unaware)

1779
01:06:44,568 --> 01:06:45,501
Okay!

1780
01:06:46,736 --> 01:06:47,636
Okay!

1781
01:06:47,637 --> 01:06:52,874
(The calm before the storm)

1782
01:06:56,045 --> 01:06:59,814
(Ready to roll)

1783
01:07:01,017 --> 01:07:02,985
Our guide, Ipu...

1784
01:07:02,986 --> 01:07:04,686
- His shirt is off.
- just took his shirt off.

1785
01:07:05,389 --> 01:07:07,423
- Wait, what is that?
- Look.

1786
01:07:07,891 --> 01:07:08,924
Do we have to wear that too?

1787
01:07:08,925 --> 01:07:10,926
- What is it?
- What is this?

1788
01:07:10,927 --> 01:07:12,595
(An accessory made of animal bones)

1789
01:07:12,828 --> 01:07:13,995
Is that your vest?

1790
01:07:14,020 --> 01:07:16,598
(Suit on)

1791
01:07:16,800 --> 01:07:18,267
- Did you make this yourself?
- Yep.

1792
01:07:19,068 --> 01:07:21,036
Yeah. Took three years.

1793
01:07:21,538 --> 01:07:23,505
- Three years?
- That took three years?

1794
01:07:24,207 --> 01:07:26,708
- Are these real bones?
- Real bones, yes.

1795
01:07:27,177 --> 01:07:29,211
- Did you hunt them?
- No.

1796
01:07:30,246 --> 01:07:31,713
Found them?

1797
01:07:31,714 --> 01:07:32,547
Yes.

1798
01:07:33,249 --> 01:07:35,317
- I think he collected them over time.
- What's this one?

1799
01:07:35,819 --> 01:07:38,020
(Looks suspiciously like teeth)

1800
01:07:38,388 --> 01:07:39,788
- Monkey.
- Monkey?

1801
01:07:39,989 --> 01:07:41,022
Monkey teeth!

1802
01:07:41,023 --> 01:07:43,258
You can see the molars.

1803
01:07:43,493 --> 01:07:46,094
He spends so much time out here.

1804
01:07:46,095 --> 01:07:47,129
I guess...

1805
01:07:47,130 --> 01:07:49,364
- he gathered them over the years.
- Feels like a protective talisman.

1806
01:07:49,365 --> 01:07:50,766
- Totally.
- Looks like...

1807
01:07:50,910 --> 01:07:51,877
(Glancing)

1808
01:07:51,902 --> 01:07:53,636
Wait, why is he taking his shoes off?

1809
01:07:54,103 --> 01:07:55,904
You're not wearing shoes?

1810
01:07:55,905 --> 01:07:56,838
Nope.

1811
01:07:57,974 --> 01:07:58,774
This is the jungle.

1812
01:07:58,775 --> 01:08:00,609
(Just another day at the office for Ipu)

1813
01:08:00,844 --> 01:08:01,944
I'm heading home.

1814
01:08:03,046 --> 01:08:04,445
So the jungle really is his home.

1815
01:08:04,446 --> 01:08:05,780
It's just like taking your shoes off...

1816
01:08:05,781 --> 01:08:07,382
- at the front door.
- That's brilliant.

1817
01:08:07,885 --> 01:08:09,851
- Unreal.
- You're amazing!

1818
01:08:09,852 --> 01:08:11,054
Now he's letting his hair down too.

1819
01:08:11,888 --> 01:08:13,689
He looks incredible.

1820
01:08:13,690 --> 01:08:14,523
(Letting his hair down at home)

1821
01:08:14,524 --> 01:08:17,659
It genuinely feels
like I'm hanging out with Tarzan.

1822
01:08:17,660 --> 01:08:18,861
- His hair.
- Real-life Tarzan.

1823
01:08:19,095 --> 01:08:21,129
Now we go to the jungle.

1824
01:08:21,130 --> 01:08:24,099
All right, now you're ready!

1825
01:08:24,100 --> 01:08:25,534
He is so badass!

1826
01:08:25,535 --> 01:08:27,704
His pre-hike routine is
on a whole different level.

1827
01:08:27,837 --> 01:08:29,839
We were out here obsessing
over what extra stuff to pack.

1828
01:08:30,540 --> 01:08:33,942
The fact that he can live out here
for a month with just that small sack...

1829
01:08:34,510 --> 01:08:36,411
That is true minimalism.

1830
01:08:36,412 --> 01:08:38,347
- Right?
- It's so cool.

1831
01:08:38,348 --> 01:08:41,549
Really makes you realize
how little you actually need to survive.

1832
01:08:41,550 --> 01:08:42,484
So true.

1833
01:08:42,485 --> 01:08:45,020
Ultimate life goals for the show.

1834
01:08:45,021 --> 01:08:47,388
Can we just recruit him permanently?

1835
01:08:48,324 --> 01:08:50,727
I feel like we could survive anywhere
with him around.

1836
01:08:50,994 --> 01:08:53,529
- Such a free spirit.
- And up we goes.

1837
01:08:54,097 --> 01:08:55,130
Completely barefoot.

1838
01:08:55,431 --> 01:08:57,665
Honestly, it looks so effortless...

1839
01:08:58,234 --> 01:09:00,068
the way he walks barefoot like that.

1840
01:09:00,069 --> 01:09:01,002
I'm kind of envious.

1841
01:09:01,404 --> 01:09:03,038
- Do you know what this is?
- Yes?

1842
01:09:04,107 --> 01:09:05,340
- Perilla leaf?
- What is it?

1843
01:09:06,843 --> 01:09:07,810
Give it a smell.

1844
01:09:08,578 --> 01:09:09,912
Oh, we can smell it from here.

1845
01:09:10,914 --> 01:09:11,814
What is that?

1846
01:09:12,815 --> 01:09:13,815
Smells leafy.

1847
01:09:14,050 --> 01:09:15,183
Interesting.

1848
01:09:15,485 --> 01:09:17,986
It's betel leaf.

1849
01:09:17,987 --> 01:09:19,354
Has a bit of a tangy scent.

1850
01:09:19,756 --> 01:09:21,857
You can rub it on mosquito bites...

1851
01:09:21,858 --> 01:09:22,991
to stop the itch.

1852
01:09:23,359 --> 01:09:24,125
(Nature's anti-itch remedy)

1853
01:09:24,126 --> 01:09:25,527
- For bug bites.
- Yeah.

1854
01:09:26,395 --> 01:09:28,063
I'm definitely asking him for some later.

1855
01:09:28,231 --> 01:09:31,266
- It's natural medicine.
- Nature really does provide everything.

1856
01:09:32,335 --> 01:09:34,503
So far it just feels
like an everyday hiking trail back home.

1857
01:09:34,504 --> 01:09:36,105
Just your average trail.

1858
01:09:36,274 --> 01:09:37,072
Totally.

1859
01:09:37,607 --> 01:09:39,908
We have tons of mountain trails
just like this in Korea.

1860
01:09:40,777 --> 01:09:42,511
The scenery still feels pretty familiar.

1861
01:09:42,512 --> 01:09:43,479
(Familiar hiking vibes so far)

1862
01:09:43,947 --> 01:09:44,980
What an adventure.

1863
01:09:45,548 --> 01:09:47,115
Seriously.

1864
01:09:47,450 --> 01:09:48,950
Totally surrounded by green.

1865
01:09:49,586 --> 01:09:50,352
(Sighs)

1866
01:09:50,353 --> 01:09:53,221
<i>Welcome to the jungle!</i>

1867
01:09:53,222 --> 01:09:55,290
(Humming)

1868
01:09:56,426 --> 01:09:58,093
(Ipu spots something.)

1869
01:09:58,094 --> 01:09:59,461
Look, he's foraging again.

1870
01:10:02,304 --> 01:10:03,480
Do you know what this is?

1871
01:10:03,481 --> 01:10:04,967
Isn't this that thing?

1872
01:10:05,301 --> 01:10:06,569
I can't remember the name.

1873
01:10:08,007 --> 01:10:09,138
It's still a young fruit.

1874
01:10:09,434 --> 01:10:10,740
It's young, but it's coffee.

1875
01:10:11,207 --> 01:10:12,347
- Coffee?
- Coffee?

1876
01:10:12,372 --> 01:10:13,543
- Robusta.
- Coffee?

1877
01:10:13,574 --> 01:10:16,075
- Is this a coffee plant?
- Yes, it's a Robusta coffee tree.

1878
01:10:16,100 --> 01:10:19,341
(A wild Robusta coffee tree)

1879
01:10:19,414 --> 01:10:22,518
Indonesia is famous for its coffee.

1880
01:10:23,342 --> 01:10:25,588
Indonesian coffee is famous. It's good.

1881
01:10:25,589 --> 01:10:27,346
(Indonesia is the world's
fourth-largest coffee producer.)

1882
01:10:27,515 --> 01:10:29,515
Coffee grows in warm climates.

1883
01:10:29,516 --> 01:10:31,894
Maybe coffee trees will start
growing in Korea now too.

1884
01:10:33,476 --> 01:10:34,597
I think they will.

1885
01:10:34,598 --> 01:10:36,263
(The stairs continue upward.)

1886
01:10:36,603 --> 01:10:37,500
(Sighing)

1887
01:10:37,656 --> 01:10:40,603
- Let me know if anyone gets tired.
- I'm okay.

1888
01:10:42,146 --> 01:10:44,051
Slowly.

1889
01:10:44,052 --> 01:10:46,576
- You can stop if you're tired.
- Okay.

1890
01:10:47,009 --> 01:10:49,612
- This isn't a competition.
- No, it's not.

1891
01:10:50,406 --> 01:10:53,330
(Ipu's mindset is admirable.)

1892
01:10:53,903 --> 01:10:57,631
- Were you born here?
- Yes.

1893
01:10:57,632 --> 01:10:59,255
You were born here.

1894
01:11:00,022 --> 01:11:01,758
I'm not from the city.

1895
01:11:02,461 --> 01:11:03,926
I'm from Borneo.

1896
01:11:04,047 --> 01:11:05,921
- Borneo.
- I grew up in the forest.

1897
01:11:06,234 --> 01:11:09,198
He grew up in the forest.

1898
01:11:10,495 --> 01:11:13,899
(Finally, the slope becomes
a little gentler.)

1899
01:11:14,626 --> 01:11:15,849
- Rubber?
- Where?

1900
01:11:15,991 --> 01:11:17,140
It's a rubber tree.

1901
01:11:17,871 --> 01:11:18,794
Rubber!

1902
01:11:20,313 --> 01:11:22,345
- It looks like a coconut shell.
- It's natural rubber.

1903
01:11:23,179 --> 01:11:24,413
Rubber tapping.

1904
01:11:24,414 --> 01:11:29,185
- They cut a groove...
- So the sap drains down.

1905
01:11:30,639 --> 01:11:33,156
I've always wanted to try tapping rubber!

1906
01:11:33,157 --> 01:11:33,856
Gabee.

1907
01:11:33,857 --> 01:11:34,846
Can we touch it?

1908
01:11:34,886 --> 01:11:36,659
Don't touch it. It smells terrible.

1909
01:11:37,019 --> 01:11:38,661
It might have a really pungent odor.

1910
01:11:38,662 --> 01:11:40,335
(The odor intensifies as it ferments.)

1911
01:11:40,595 --> 01:11:42,131
I still kind of want to touch it.

1912
01:11:42,862 --> 01:11:44,131
I'm dying to know
what the texture feels like.

1913
01:11:44,155 --> 01:11:46,669
- This is real-deal natural rubber.
- Pure rubber.

1914
01:11:48,143 --> 01:11:49,443
(Pokes)

1915
01:11:49,610 --> 01:11:50,807
I want to try it.

1916
01:11:51,997 --> 01:11:53,277
(Blegh)

1917
01:11:53,761 --> 01:11:54,627
(Yuck)

1918
01:11:54,843 --> 01:11:56,612
I never imagined it would smell like this.

1919
01:11:57,543 --> 01:11:59,270
(Traded a nose mole
for a dab of rubber sap)

1920
01:11:59,743 --> 01:12:01,470
(The pungent rubber smell hits hard.)

1921
01:12:01,930 --> 01:12:03,286
You got it right on your nose!

1922
01:12:03,586 --> 01:12:05,188
It honestly smells like poop.

1923
01:12:05,294 --> 01:12:07,690
More like a funky, fermented smell.

1924
01:12:08,094 --> 01:12:09,025
Very funky.

1925
01:12:09,026 --> 01:12:10,812
- Look at her looking on the bright side.
- Not urine.

1926
01:12:10,813 --> 01:12:13,396
Yeah, not pee. Straight-up poop.

1927
01:12:13,452 --> 01:12:14,730
This is so wild.

1928
01:12:15,306 --> 01:12:16,666
Wait, hold on a second.

1929
01:12:16,667 --> 01:12:19,068
I think he feels bad for you.

1930
01:12:19,093 --> 01:12:20,736
(Ipu sweet-naturedly
wipes it off for her.)

1931
01:12:21,480 --> 01:12:22,547
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

1932
01:12:22,548 --> 01:12:25,208
I actually braced for it
to smell way worse.

1933
01:12:26,247 --> 01:12:27,977
There are so many rubber trees here.

1934
01:12:28,633 --> 01:12:30,227
(A dense forest of rubber trees)

1935
01:12:30,260 --> 01:12:32,114
I guess rubber is a major local crop.

1936
01:12:32,515 --> 01:12:34,300
(Rubber sap buckets
hanging all over the forest)

1937
01:12:34,301 --> 01:12:35,684
I want to try tapping one
on the hike down!

1938
01:12:35,793 --> 01:12:38,647
I feel like I'm learning
so much on this trip.

1939
01:12:38,648 --> 01:12:39,889
That rubber chunk looks hideous.

1940
01:12:40,133 --> 01:12:41,357
This feels amazing.

1941
01:12:41,593 --> 01:12:44,393
- Proper hiking vibes.
- It really does feel great.

1942
01:12:45,399 --> 01:12:48,844
It hasn't gotten too steep yet,
so we can actually take in the views.

1943
01:12:48,845 --> 01:12:50,385
(A mercifully gentle stretch of trail)

1944
01:12:50,718 --> 01:12:52,101
I love this so much.

1945
01:12:52,198 --> 01:12:53,336
Feels like...

1946
01:12:53,904 --> 01:12:55,503
we completely left the city behind...

1947
01:12:55,905 --> 01:12:58,140
and melted right into nature.

1948
01:12:59,310 --> 01:13:01,376
(Cringe warning)

1949
01:13:01,543 --> 01:13:02,478
Total soul cleanse...

1950
01:13:02,503 --> 01:13:04,046
Wait, look over there!

1951
01:13:04,047 --> 01:13:05,081
This trail is gorgeous.

1952
01:13:05,082 --> 01:13:06,782
It looks like Thanos' retirement garden.

1953
01:13:07,067 --> 01:13:08,451
This is unbelievable.

1954
01:13:09,719 --> 01:13:11,654
- What is this place?
- It's breathtaking.

1955
01:13:13,089 --> 01:13:14,628
(A picturesque, fairytale-like cottage)

1956
01:13:14,653 --> 01:13:17,353
It looks straight out
of an animated movie.

1957
01:13:17,354 --> 01:13:19,528
Can we just crash here tonight?

1958
01:13:20,047 --> 01:13:22,131
I wish this were our campsite.

1959
01:13:22,200 --> 01:13:23,232
Seriously, no kidding.

1960
01:13:23,567 --> 01:13:25,148
Who knew a place like this
existed deep in the jungle?

1961
01:13:25,173 --> 01:13:26,135
Unreal.

1962
01:13:30,267 --> 01:13:31,807
Number Three, how are you holding up?

1963
01:13:33,142 --> 01:13:35,645
Why does this feel
like a dating reality show?

1964
01:13:35,646 --> 01:13:39,173
(Contestant No. 3 running low on stamina)

1965
01:13:39,639 --> 01:13:40,750
Do you know this fruit?

1966
01:13:40,751 --> 01:13:42,514
(Ipu picks a tiny fruit for her.)

1967
01:13:42,539 --> 01:13:43,821
Is this a mini tangerine?

1968
01:13:43,846 --> 01:13:44,720
(A fresh blast of citrus lime)

1969
01:13:44,721 --> 01:13:45,988
- It's a lime!
- A wild lime.

1970
01:13:46,233 --> 01:13:47,857
That smells incredible.

1971
01:13:47,858 --> 01:13:49,858
It smells so refreshing.

1972
01:13:50,526 --> 01:13:52,094
Lime.

1973
01:13:52,713 --> 01:13:54,797
- Lime.
- Lime.

1974
01:13:54,906 --> 01:13:57,800
This works way better
than a yadom inhaler.

1975
01:13:57,801 --> 01:13:59,368
- Forget the yadom.
- Yes, forget it.

1976
01:13:59,906 --> 01:14:01,906
- Good?
- Totally.

1977
01:14:01,913 --> 01:14:03,606
- Yadom.
- Yadom.

1978
01:14:04,506 --> 01:14:06,809
- Yar.
- Yar.

1979
01:14:07,944 --> 01:14:09,211
His accent is so charming.

1980
01:14:09,545 --> 01:14:12,214
Whatever he says just sounds so cool.

1981
01:14:12,782 --> 01:14:14,317
We're heading downhill now.

1982
01:14:14,358 --> 01:14:15,631
Nice, a downhill stretch.

1983
01:14:16,635 --> 01:14:18,220
The brush is getting pretty thick.

1984
01:14:19,622 --> 01:14:22,242
Now it's starting to feel
like a real jungle.

1985
01:14:22,243 --> 01:14:23,484
The grass is getting way taller.

1986
01:14:23,509 --> 01:14:25,661
Look how high it comes up now.

1987
01:14:29,649 --> 01:14:31,271
Look, he's showing us something else.

1988
01:14:31,272 --> 01:14:34,570
- Ipu isn't even breaking a sweat.
- The man is a walking encyclopedia.

1989
01:14:34,571 --> 01:14:36,466
(Ipu's playful expression
turns dead serious.)

1990
01:14:36,999 --> 01:14:38,646
(Over there!)

1991
01:14:40,508 --> 01:14:42,045
I think there's something over there.

1992
01:14:43,293 --> 01:14:45,293
Wait, I hear rustling.

1993
01:14:45,915 --> 01:14:47,683
Let's check it out.

1994
01:14:48,242 --> 01:14:49,051
Let's check it out.

1995
01:14:49,229 --> 01:14:52,002
(Did something just appear?)

1996
01:14:52,049 --> 01:14:53,255
Where?

1997
01:14:55,874 --> 01:14:57,884
(Shh)

1998
01:15:02,107 --> 01:15:04,900
(Gasps)

1999
01:15:05,601 --> 01:15:06,702
No way.

2000
01:15:07,408 --> 01:15:08,988
Are you serious?

2001
01:15:08,989 --> 01:15:10,172
Right over there!

2002
01:15:10,539 --> 01:15:12,388
(A mysterious creature
emerges from the canopy.)

2003
01:15:12,414 --> 01:15:13,743
We're surrounded.

2004
01:15:14,254 --> 01:15:17,713
They're over here, and over there too.

2005
01:15:17,788 --> 01:15:19,788
We're completely boxed in.

2006
01:15:20,174 --> 01:15:21,417
Right there?

2007
01:15:23,819 --> 01:15:25,087
Wait a second...

2008
01:15:26,630 --> 01:15:28,743
(What did they just stumble into?)

2009
01:15:28,790 --> 01:15:29,959
This is insane.

2010
01:15:32,677 --> 01:15:35,423
(The real jungle survival begins.)

2011
01:15:35,710 --> 01:15:40,097
(Pushing deeper
through the dense brush and vines)

2012
01:15:40,430 --> 01:15:41,403
(Did they spot something?)

2013
01:15:41,983 --> 01:15:43,522
We're super close now.

2014
01:15:43,868 --> 01:15:46,488
(The true masters of the jungle
reveal themselves.)

2015
01:15:46,761 --> 01:15:48,047
There are more up in the canopy!

2016
01:15:48,071 --> 01:15:49,501
So many of them!

2017
01:15:50,713 --> 01:15:53,215
(The four travelers,
cornered by jungle royalty)

2018
01:15:53,435 --> 01:15:55,422
- There are so many of them.
- Look at the branches shaking.

2019
01:15:55,595 --> 01:15:56,415
Wait, hold on!

2020
01:15:56,662 --> 01:15:58,922
(A panicked cry breaks the silence.)

2021
01:15:59,388 --> 01:16:00,422
(Are they closing in on us?)

2022
01:16:00,628 --> 01:16:03,542
(A warning shot from the wild?)

2023
01:16:05,582 --> 01:16:07,682
(Absolute chaos)

2024
01:16:08,288 --> 01:16:09,528
(Total panic)

2025
01:16:09,762 --> 01:16:10,875
Hey, that's mine!

2026
01:16:11,482 --> 01:16:13,782
(A raw battle for survival kicks off.)

2027
01:16:14,235 --> 01:16:15,682
(Shocked)

2028
01:16:16,135 --> 01:16:18,695
(Can these city girls make it
through the untamed wild?)

2029
01:16:19,015 --> 01:16:20,895
(The reality of their jungle camp
is finally revealed.)

2030
01:16:21,348 --> 01:16:23,000
Here's your room.

2031
01:16:23,214 --> 01:16:26,680
(A cozy little four-person jungle tent)

2032
01:16:27,007 --> 01:16:28,694
You've got to be kidding me.

2033
01:16:29,051 --> 01:16:30,794
I have never slept in conditions
like this in my entire life.

2034
01:16:30,974 --> 01:16:31,907
No problem?

2035
01:16:32,127 --> 01:16:34,918
(The most chaotic camping night
is about to unfold.)

2036
01:16:35,550 --> 01:16:38,191
What stood out the most to you today?

2037
01:16:38,192 --> 01:16:39,285
The swim.

2038
01:16:39,465 --> 01:16:41,897
Was there really nothing good
about spending time with us?

2039
01:16:41,985 --> 01:16:44,963
(The brutal truth
finally slips out on Day 7.)

2040
01:16:44,988 --> 01:16:51,036
Still, as the oldest one in this group...

2041
01:16:51,109 --> 01:16:52,370
Wait, is she tearing up?

2042
01:16:52,395 --> 01:16:54,243
- Are you crying?
- Seriously?

2043
01:16:54,403 --> 01:16:56,812
To be completely honest with you guys...

2044
01:16:57,400 --> 01:17:01,016
(Next week, the raw, tearful truth
is finally revealed.)

2045
01:17:01,041 --> 01:17:02,466
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
